      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486788055": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "It's fun to work in a company where people truly BELIEVE in what they're doing!\nWe're committed to bringing passion and customer focus to the business.\nAt Cisive, our vision is to make securing the right talent effortless. We provide technology-first background screening, identity verification, and continuous monitoring solutions that help organizations hire and manage their workforce with confidence.\nOur Values\nIntegrity First: We uphold the highest ethical standards in everything we do.\nInnovate Fearlessly: We challenge the status quo, embrace emerging technologies, and continuously refine our solutions to stay ahead of industry needs.\nWin Together: We break down barriers, share knowledge, and champion teamwork across departments, brands, and global offices to achieve our collective goals.\nCustomer Obsessed: We go beyond transactional interactions to become trusted partners in risk mitigation and workforce management.\nStay One Step Ahead: We proactively seek knowledge that helps us—and our clients—stay ahead of the curve\nJob Summary\nThe Associate Software Developer is an entry-level role responsible for supporting the development, testing, and maintenance of software applications under the guidance of senior team members. This position focuses on building foundational programming skills, contributing to team development efforts, and learning industry best practices while supporting Cisive’s enterprise software platforms.\nDuties And Responsibilities\nWrite clean, maintainable, and efficient code following established coding standards.\nAssist in identifying, troubleshooting, and resolving basic software defects.\nParticipate in code reviews to learn best practices and support continuous improvement.\nCollaborate with team members to design, develop, and test new or enhanced software features.\nSupport the documentation of code, technical processes, and application functionality.\nContribute to Agile ceremonies including sprint planning, sprint reviews, and daily stand-ups.\nLearn and apply new technologies, frameworks, and tools as directed by senior development staff.\nPerform other duties as assigned.\nMinimum Qualifications\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related field (or equivalent practical experience).\n0–2 years of professional software development experience.\nBasic proficiency in at least one programming language (e.g., C#, Java, Python).\nUnderstanding of core software development concepts such as algorithms, data structures, debugging, and version control.\nStrong analytical and problem‑solving skills with an eagerness to learn.\nEffective communication skills and ability to collaborate within a team environment.\nWorking Conditions\nFully remote work environment.\nCollaborative, team-oriented setting with guidance and mentorship from senior engineers.\nUse of modern software development tools, repositories, and cloud-based platforms.\nPhysical Requirements\nAbility to communicate clearly and exchange accurate information frequently.\nConstant operation of a computer, keyboard, phone, and other standard office equipment.\nAbility to occasionally move objects up to 10 lbs.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487688718": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This position is listed on behalf of a partner company, who manages all applications and next steps. Our partner is looking for a Backend Software Engineer (Node.js) | LabArchives based in the United States.\nThe Backend Software Engineer will contribute to the development and evolution of innovative scientific software solutions used by researchers and institutions worldwide. You will join a dedicated engineering team responsible for building and maintaining the backend systems powering Electronic Laboratory Notebook (ELN), Inventory, and Scheduler products. Working primarily with Node.js, you will design scalable services and APIs while contributing to existing Ruby on Rails applications. You will collaborate closely with product, operations, and support teams to deliver reliable, high-quality software. This role offers significant technical ownership, opportunities to improve engineering processes, and exposure to a global SaaS environment. Your work will directly support scientific research, technological innovation, and the advancement of digital laboratory solutions.\nAccountabilities\nResponsibilities\nAs a Backend Software Engineer, you will design, develop, and maintain backend applications and services while contributing to product quality, performance, and scalability. Your responsibilities will include:\nCollaborate with product, operations, and support teams to design, develop, and maintain backend services and APIs.\nBuild and deliver new backend features primarily using Node.js.\nPlan, implement, test, and release software improvements through an iterative development process.\nRead, understand, maintain, and contribute to the existing Ruby on Rails codebase when required.\nDevelop and maintain comprehensive unit tests to ensure software reliability and quality.\nParticipate in building and expanding automated testing frameworks.\nConduct and contribute to code reviews, security audits, and performance evaluations.\nAssess application scalability and identify opportunities to improve backend architecture and system efficiency.\nApply best practices in database development, API design, and software engineering.\nCollaborate across departments to continuously improve development workflows, technical processes, and product capabilities.\nRequirements\nThe ideal candidate is an experienced backend engineer with strong technical expertise, a passion for software development, and the ability to collaborate across multidisciplinary teams. You should demonstrate a continuous learning mindset and be comfortable working with established codebases and evolving technologies. Key qualifications include:\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and professional experience.\nAt least 9 years of relevant professional experience.\nStrong hands-on experience with server-side development using Node.js.\nProven ability to build, maintain, and integrate backend APIs and services.\nExperience with both synchronous and asynchronous integration patterns.\nAbility to read, understand, and work with Ruby code; experience with Ruby on Rails is preferred.\nSolid understanding of database design, data modeling, and query optimization.\nStrong knowledge of object-oriented and functional programming principles.\nProficiency in modern JavaScript (ES6+) and RESTful API design.\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, and debugging skills.\nExcellent communication and collaboration abilities, with experience working across multiple departments.\nEnthusiasm for technology, continuous improvement, and learning new tools and practices.\nPreferred Qualifications\nExperience developing SaaS products, particularly in regulated, scientific, or research-focused industries.\nFamiliarity with automated testing tools, test frameworks, and CI/CD pipelines.\nUnderstanding of security best practices and secure API development, including authentication, authorization, and data protection.\nBasic familiarity with frontend frameworks such as React, Angular, or Vue.js.\nInterest in scientific or educational technology and its role in advancing research and discovery.\nBenefits\nSalary: $103,000–$140,000 USD annually, depending on experience, qualifications, skills, and location.\nCompetitive total rewards package combining compensation, benefits, and recognition.\nMedical, dental, and vision insurance.\nHealth Spending Accounts.\nWellness benefits, including mental health applications and fitness perks.\nCompany-paid life and disability insurance.\n401(k) retirement plan with a 4% employer match and immediate vesting.\nFlexible paid time off plan for U.S. exempt employees.\nPotential eligibility for additional variable compensation, depending on the position.\nRemote-friendly and collaborative working environment.\nOpportunities to contribute to innovative scientific technologies and work alongside a global team.\nHow Jobgether Works\nWe use an AI-powered matching process to ensure your application is reviewed quickly, objectively, and fairly against the role's core requirements. Our system identifies the top-fitting candidates, and this shortlist is then shared directly with the hiring company. The final decision and next steps (interviews, assessments) are managed by their internal team.\nWe appreciate your interest and wish you the best!\nWhy Apply Through Jobgether?\nData Privacy Notice: By submitting your application, you acknowledge that Jobgether will process your personal data to evaluate your candidacy and share relevant information with the hiring employer. This processing is based on legitimate interest and pre-contractual measures under applicable data protection laws (including GDPR). You may exercise your rights (access, rectification, erasure, objection) at any time.\nWe may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses and identifying potential inconsistencies or verification signals in application materials based on available information. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488245671": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThe organization operates in the technology sector, focusing on developing software solutions that meet project requirements and improve existing systems. It addresses the challenge of building reliable, scalable, and efficient technology by applying strong software development principles and collaborative engineering practices. The organization emphasizes practical software development and continuous learning within a team environment.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE DEVELOPER is responsible for contributing to the development, testing, and maintenance of software applications. This role supports the organization by applying programming knowledge and problem-solving skills to build and enhance software solutions that meet business objectives. It offers an opportunity to work on real-world technical challenges and develop practical software products while growing technical expertise.\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop, test, debug, and maintain software applications based on project requirements.\nWrite clean, efficient, reusable, and maintainable code following best practices.\nCollaborate with developers and cross-functional team members to design and implement features.\nUse programming languages such as Python, Java, JavaScript, or TypeScript.\nAssist in developing and integrating REST APIs and web application components.\nWork with databases and SQL to manage application data.\nIdentify and troubleshoot software defects and performance issues.\nParticipate in code reviews and incorporate feedback.\nUse Git and GitHub for version control.\nWrite and execute unit tests to ensure software reliability.\nDocument technical processes, features, and workflows.\nLearn and apply new tools, frameworks, and technologies.\nRequirements:\nMaster's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, Computer Engineering, or related field.\n0–1 year of experience in Software Engineering, Software Development, or related role.\nStrong understanding of programming fundamentals and object-oriented programming.\nProficiency in at least one programming language such as Python, Java, JavaScript, or TypeScript.\nFamiliarity with data structures and algorithms.\nUnderstanding of REST APIs and web application fundamentals.\nFamiliarity with SQL, relational databases, and basic database concepts.\nExperience using Git and GitHub for version control.\nUnderstanding of software development life cycle principles.\nFamiliarity with debugging, testing, and writing maintainable code.\nStrong analytical thinking and problem-solving abilities.\nAbility to learn new technologies and adapt to project requirements.\nStrong communication, teamwork, and collaboration skills.\nMotivation to build reliable software and continuously improve technical skills.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nThe pay range and compensation package for this role will be determined based on the candidate's experience, skills, and other relevant factors.\nAbout the Opportunity (Preferred Qualifications):\nExperience with academic, internship, or personal software development projects.\nFamiliarity with frontend frameworks like React or backend frameworks like Node.js, Django, or Spring Boot.\nBasic knowledge of cloud platforms, software deployment, or CI/CD.\nFamiliarity with Agile development and collaborative workflows.\nOpportunity to work with modern development tools and engineering practices.\nCollaborative environment promoting knowledge sharing and continuous learning.\nOpportunities for professional development and career growth.\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488260122": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThis organization operates in the AI data platform industry, addressing challenges related to sourcing and preparing proprietary, high-quality data across video, audio, text, and business workflows for AI training and evaluation. It provides a licensed platform that indexes, enriches, and packages this scarce data to support AI labs and model builders in developing next-generation AI models. The team is small but impactful, backed by top investors, and focused on solving significant bottlenecks in AI development.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe FRONTEND ENGINEER will build and maintain web applications used by customers and internal teams, contributing to the delivery of reliable and polished software products. The role involves working across the frontend stack, collaborating closely with design, product, and backend teams to ensure high-quality user experiences. This position is important for enabling the organization to provide effective tools and interfaces that facilitate AI data handling and modeling.\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop features for customer-facing and internal web applications in environments integrated with Rails as well as standalone frameworks\nMaintain and enhance the shared component library, including documentation and accessibility\nImplement designs with accuracy and provide constructive feedback on design specifications\nOptimize application performance focusing on rendering, bundle size, and handling large data sets\nMaintain and extend test coverage\nTroubleshoot production issues using monitoring tools\nRequirements:\nMinimum of 5 years experience building production web interfaces with React and TypeScript\nProficient in HTML, CSS, responsive layouts, and Tailwind\nSkilled at working directly from Figma files and collaborating with designers\nExperience integrating REST APIs and managing authentication and various UI states\nFamiliarity with testing frameworks such as Vitest, Jest, or Playwright\nUnderstanding of coding agents and their practical application\nClear written communication with cross-functional teams\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nBase Salary: $130,000 to $165,000 depending on experience and location\nEquity: Competitive equity package within a well-funded AI startup\nBenefits & Perks:\nMedical, dental, and vision coverage fully paid by the employer for employees\nFlexible paid time off policy with encouragement to use it\nRemote-first work policy with occasional team offsites\nAnnual learning stipend and access to conferences\nEquity ownership with growth potential\nBudget for modern equipment and software\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488281825": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThis organization operates in the technology sector, specializing in Apple device management solutions. It addresses the challenge of efficiently managing Apple devices across enterprises by providing tools that support over 75,000 global customers. The program supports continuous innovation and adapts quickly to new Apple operating system releases, fostering a community of IT professionals and developers.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe ASSOCIATE SOFTWARE ENGINEER (FULL STACK) role focuses on developing software tools that enable organizations to succeed with Apple products. This position contributes by collaborating with experienced engineers and product teams to deliver impactful features and enhancements. The role supports the organization's mission by ensuring high-quality software delivery and maintaining product expertise.\nResponsibilities:\nCollaborate with experienced engineers and product management\nBuild and maintain software tools related to Apple device management\nFollow engineering best practices and processes\nPartner with senior engineers to learn technical concepts\nMaintain a positive attitude while addressing challenges\nParticipate in periodic onsite collaboration as needed\nRequirements:\nMinimum of one year experience in enterprise-grade software development (preferred)\nExperience with Java, Kotlin, or TypeScript (preferred)\nFamiliarity with Angular or other front-end frameworks (preferred)\nKnowledge of Agile development practices (preferred)\nExposure to AWS services, including DynamoDB (preferred)\nUnderstanding of containers such as Docker and GitHub Actions (preferred)\nExperience with AI-driven coding assistants like GitHub Copilot (preferred)\nHigh school diploma or GED (required)\nBachelor's degree or equivalent experience (preferred)\nCommitment to ongoing security training and adherence to security protocols\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nNational pay transparency range: $64,800 to $117,480 USD, depending on location and other factors\nBenefits & Perks:\nMedical insurance\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488287763": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThe organization operates in the education technology sector, providing tech-enabled learning solutions focused on increasing access to flexible learning environments for students and equipping educators with effective tools. It addresses challenges in educational delivery by partnering with educators to develop proven learning technologies. As a remote-first entity, the company emphasizes innovation and customer satisfaction while supporting a wide range of educational stakeholders.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER I will contribute to the development and maintenance of learning technology solutions. This role is responsible for supporting the technical implementation of products that enhance educational experiences, ensuring that the organization's tools effectively meet the needs of educators and students. The position plays a critical role in sustaining and improving the technology that underpins the organization's mission.\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop, test, and maintain software applications supporting educational tools.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to deliver high-quality technology solutions.\nParticipate in code reviews and contribute to continuous improvement of development processes.\nTroubleshoot and resolve technical issues as they arise.\nSupport deployment and integration of software updates.\nRequirements:\nRelevant degree or equivalent experience in software development.\nProficiency in programming languages and software development methodologies.\nAbility to work collaboratively in a remote team environment.\nStrong problem-solving and communication skills.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nThe pay range for this role is $80,000 to $100,000 USD.\nBenefits & Perks:\nMedical insurance with various plan options.\nDental insurance.\nVision insurance.\n401(k) retirement plan with company matching.\nTime away programs including volunteer time off and a winter office closure.\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488295678": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Our client growing technology company focused on developing modern software applications, scalable web platforms, and innovative digital solutions. We are looking for motivated developers who want to grow their technical skills while contributing to real-world projects.\nMust be Us Citizen\nSalary: 80,000 USD Yearly\nResponsibilities\nDevelop, test, and maintain web applications.\nWork with frontend and backend technologies.\nWrite clean, reusable, and maintainable code.\nCollaborate with engineers on feature development.\nTroubleshoot bugs and improve application performance.\nParticipate in code reviews and team discussions.\nLearn and apply modern development tools and practices.\nRequirements\n0–2 years of software development experience.\nBasic knowledge of JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Java, or C#.\nFamiliarity with React, Node.js, or similar frameworks.\nUnderstanding of REST APIs and databases.\nFamiliarity with Git and GitHub.\nStrong problem-solving and communication skills.\nComputer Science degree, equivalent training, or relevant project experience.\nNice to Have\nExperience with AWS or other cloud platforms.\nFamiliarity with Docker and CI/CD.\nPersonal projects or open-source contributions.\nExperience using AI coding tools such as Cursor, Claude, or GitHub Copilot.\nWhat We Offer\nFully remote work opportunities.\nMentorship from experienced engineers.\nHands-on experience with production software.\nFlexible and collaborative work environment.\nOpportunities for professional growth.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
