        "payload": {
          "description": "Ghosted After Applying: Candidates Tired of Silence\nGhosting Is Now the Default. It Does Not Have to Be Your Default.\nYou apply, sometimes complete a HackerRank, and then nothing. No rejection, no recruiter, no feedback. Data engineer roles are competitive, and companies ghost candidates who look generic: some SQL, some Python, no pipeline narrative, no cloud, no Spark. Silence is a market signal that your profile is not being championed.\nMake Your Profile Impossible to Ignore\nWhy You’re Being Overlooked—and How We Can Help\nMany employers today don’t just want a degree—they’re looking for job-ready developers with hands-on experience, relevant certifications, and up-to-date skills in today’s tech stack. Unfortunately, most CS grads don’t get that in college.\nSince 2010, we’ve helped thousands of candidates land full-time jobs at tech leaders like Google, Apple, PayPal, Visa, Western Union, Wells Fargo, Intel, Paypal, JPMC, Wayfair, BOA, CITI and hundreds more with Job offers of $95k to $154k. Synergisticit focuses on closing the gap between your tech skills and what employers want now.\nCurrently, We are looking for entry-level software programmers, Java Full stack developers, Python/Java developers, Data analysts/Data Engineers/ Data Scientists, Machine Learning engineers for full time positions with clients.\nWe Focus on Java /Full stack/Devops and Data Science /Data Engineers/Data analysts/BI Analysts/ Machine learning/AI candidates\nIdeal Candidates:\nRecent grads in CS, Engineering, Math, or Statistics with limited or no job experience\nJobseekers who had layoffs due to Downsizing and want to get in demand tech stack\nProfessionals seeking a career switch to tech\nCandidates with career gaps or lacking real-world experience\nIndividuals looking to boost their skill portfolio for better job prospects\nComputer Science grads with limited or no job experience\nStudents who recently finished their Bachelor’s or Master’s programs\nThose struggling to land interviews despite having experience\nPlease check the below links:\nEvent videos (OCW, JavaOne, Gartner):\nUSA Today feature\nDiscover JOPP: JOPP\nReviews : https://www.synergisticit.com/reviews/\nplease read our blogs:\nWhy do Tech Companies not Hire recent Computer Science Graduates | SynergisticIT\nWhat Recruiters Look for in Junior Developers | SynergisticIT\nIs AI Going to Replace Software Programmers? | SynergisticIT\nAimed at Direct Full-Time Roles\nSynergisticit emphasizes interviews for direct clients and full-time positions rather than contract chains. Salary outcomes from about $95k to $154k, with data hires associated with firms such as Intel, Citi, JPMC, Ford, and Walmart Labs.\nIf your current process is apply-and-wait, you already know the result.\nReplace ghosting with scheduled interviews. When nothing else works, JOPP works\nPlease note: Resume databases are shared with clients and interested clients will reach out directly if they find a qualified candidate for their req.\nResume submissions may be shared with our JOPP team database also. Please unsubscribe if contacted or if you don’t want to be contacted please don’t submit your resume.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489059039": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Three Hundred Applications, Zero Recruiter Calls\nVolume Is Not a Strategy When Nobody Opens the Resume\nYou track applications in a spreadsheet. The number looks impressive. The callback count is zero. ATS filters, keyword mismatches, and sourcers who never see your name are not mysteries. They are the default. If you cannot get Java interviews, the market is not “ignoring talent.” It is ignoring an unmarketed, unproven profile.\nSynergisticIT exists for jobseekers who cannot break the first-round wall. After skills, projects, and interview readiness, the team markets you to clients instead of leaving distribution to Easy Apply.\nMake the Resume Worth Opening\nJava hiring or Data Engineer/Data Science hiring still tests Core Java, Spring Boot, microservices, SQL, DSA, Snowflake, Gen AI, LLM, Rag, and cloud/DevOps, MLOPS. Synergisticit rebuilds those skills, assigns enterprise-style projects, and prepares certifications companies still use as filters. Mock interviews stop you from wasting the rare screen you finally get.\nThis is the opposite of sending the same PDF 300 times. You change the product, then someone sells it.\nAt SynergisticIT , we specialize in helping candidates like you regain momentum, rebuild confidence, and get hired.\nWhy You’re Being Overlooked—and How We Can Help\nMany employers today don’t just want a degree—they’re looking for job-ready developers with hands-on experience, relevant certifications, and up-to-date skills in today’s tech stack. Unfortunately, most CS grads don’t get that in college.\nSince 2010, we’ve helped thousands of candidates land full-time jobs at tech leaders like Google, Apple, PayPal, Visa, Western Union, Wells Fargo, Intel, Paypal, JPMC, Wayfair, BOA, CITI and hundreds more with Job offers of $95k to $154k. Synergisticit focuses on closing the gap between your tech skills and what employers want now.\nCurrently, We are looking for entry-level software programmers, Java Full stack developers, Python/Java developers, Data analysts/Data Engineers/ Data Scientists, Machine Learning engineers for full time positions with clients.\nWe Focus on Java /Full stack/Devops and Data Science /Data Engineers/Data analysts/BI Analysts/ Machine learning/AI candidates\nIdeal Candidates:\nRecent grads in CS, Engineering, Math, or Statistics with limited or no job experience\nJobseekers who had layoffs due to Downsizing and want to get in demand tech stack\nProfessionals seeking a career switch to tech\nCandidates with career gaps or lacking real-world experience\nIndividuals looking to boost their skill portfolio for better job prospects\nComputer Science grads with limited or no job experience\nStudents who recently finished their Bachelor’s or Master’s programs\nThose struggling to land interviews despite having experience\nPlease check the below links:\nEvent videos (OCW, JavaOne, Gartner):\nUSA Today feature\nDiscover JOPP: JOPP\nReviews : https://www.synergisticit.com/reviews/\nplease read our blogs:\nWhy do Tech Companies not Hire recent Computer Science Graduates | SynergisticIT\nWhat Recruiters Look for in Junior Developers | SynergisticIT\nIs AI Going to Replace Software Programmers? | SynergisticIT\nInterviews Come From updated tech skills + Aggressive Marketing, Not Hope\nGet hired with Visa, Apple, PayPal, Walmart Labs, AutoZone, Wells Fargo, Capital One, Bank of America, SAP, Verizon, T-Mobile, Intuit, Ford, and Deloitte. Salaries often range $95k–$154k.\nIf the spreadsheet is growing and the phone is not, change the system.\nStop counting applications. Start getting interviews. When nothing else works, JOPP works\nPlease note: Resume databases are shared with clients and interested clients will reach out directly if they find a qualified candidate for their req.\nResume submissions may be shared with our JOPP team database also. Please unsubscribe if contacted or if you don’t want to be contacted please don’t submit your resume.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
