      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489201807": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Role Title : Fullstack Software Engineer (Remote)\nRole Type : Full-time\nLocation : Remote\nThe Role\nThis is an AI-native fullstack engineering role building micro1's human data platforms. You'll own features end-to-end, from backend services and data pipelines to the frontends our experts use every day.\nThe role sits between traditional fullstack and research engineering. Coding agents are your primary development workflow, and you'll work closely with research engineers, operations, and product to turn requirements into reliable production systems.\nWhat You'll Own\n1. Design and ship fullstack features across backend APIs, data pipelines, and React frontends.\n2. Own client-facing data delivery and platform infrastructure, including exports, access control, and reliability.\n3. Scope work around outcomes, direct coding agents—often in parallel—review changes at the architecture level, and iterate until shipped.\n4. Build and maintain services in Python (FastAPI) and TypeScript.\n5. Contribute to data modeling, schema design, and query performance across relational and document databases.\n6. Partner with research engineering, operations, and product to translate platform needs into production-ready systems.\n7. Improve the frameworks, checks, and evals that make agent-driven development faster without sacrificing quality.\n8. Troubleshoot production issues and build resilient, observable systems.\nWhat We're Looking For\n1. Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.\n2. 0–5 years of software engineering experience, or strong shipped projects as a recent graduate.\n3. Strong fundamentals in Python and TypeScript, with experience building CRUD applications using frameworks such as FastAPI/Flask and React.\n4. Working knowledge of databases such as PostgreSQL, MongoDB, or SQLite and core data modeling principles.\n5. Experience deploying services on a major cloud platform (GCP, AWS, or Azure).\n6. Coding agents such as Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex are your default development workflow, and you can clearly explain how you use them.\n7. Ability to turn outcomes into plans, direct agents, verify results, and identify architectural issues agents may miss.\n8. Understanding of agent loops, MCP, tool/data integrations, permissions, and security.\n9. Familiarity with context management, RAG, and evals for testing agent workflows.\nPreferred\n1. Exposure to RL concepts or environments, including tasks, actions, and rewards.\n2. Experience with coding data pipelines or task-authoring platforms.\n3. Familiarity with CI/CD, deployment pipelines, and DevOps fundamentals.\n4. Experience contributing to team projects, open-source software, or startups.\nThe national pay range for this full-time position is a base salary of $120,000 - $160,000 per year. All employees are eligible for equity compensation, and employees may also receive performance-based bonuses, dependent on role and subject to company policies. micro1 provides a comprehensive benefits package, including up to 100% reimbursement for health-insurance premiums, paid time off, a 401(K) plan with a company match, and additional benefits designed to support a high-performing, remote-first workforce.\nmicro1 is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, or gender identity), national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable local laws, regulations and ordinances. If you need assistance and/or a reasonable accommodation during the application process, reach out to support@micro1.ai.\nOur hiring process utilizes artificial intelligence tools to assist in candidate screening and assessment. Our AI tools are designed to complement, not replace, human decision-making.\nWhat You’ll Do\n1. Design and ship fullstack features across backend APIs, data pipelines, and React frontends.\n2. Own client-facing data delivery and platform infrastructure, including exports, access control, and reliability.\n3. Scope work around outcomes, direct coding agents—often in parallel—review changes at the architecture level, and iterate until shipped.\n4. Build and maintain services in Python (FastAPI) and TypeScript.\n5. Contribute to data modeling, schema design, and query performance across relational and document databases.\n6. Partner with research engineering, operations, and product to translate platform needs into production-ready systems.\nApply Now!",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489354567": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Description Place of Website is a digital solutions provider focused on helping businesses, professionals, and individuals build a strong online presence. The company offers full stack development, logo and graphic design, SEO and content creation, hosting, domain services, and website design and development courses. With a commitment to expert, affordable, and customized services, Place of Website supports both startups and established organizations in achieving their digital goals. The team emphasizes educational support and customer-focused collaboration to turn ideas into practical, impactful web experiences.\nRole Description The PHP Developer role at Place of Website is a part-time remote position focused on building and maintaining web applications and sites. Day-to-day responsibilities include writing clean, efficient PHP code, implementing back-end functionality, integrating front-end components, and working with databases to ensure secure and stable performance. The developer will collaborate with designers and other team members to implement features, troubleshoot issues, optimize existing code, and support enhancements to client projects and internal platforms. The role also involves testing, debugging, and ensuring code quality and scalability in line with best practices and project requirements.\nQualifications\nCandidates should possess strong Back-End Web Development and Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) skills.\nCandidates should possess Front-End Development skills to effectively integrate user interfaces with PHP back-end logic.\nCandidates should possess solid Software Development and Programming skills, including familiarity with version control and debugging tools.\nCandidates should possess experience working with PHP frameworks (such as Laravel or Symfony) and relational databases (such as MySQL).\nCandidates should possess knowledge of web standards, security best practices, and RESTful APIs.\nCandidates should possess effective communication skills, the ability to work independently in a remote setting, and strong problem-solving abilities.\nA relevant degree or equivalent practical experience in computer science, software engineering, or web development is beneficial.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489987337": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Node.js Developer\nCompany: HAN Staffing\nListed location: Iselin, NJ 08830\nRole locations noted in the job details: Irving, TX, or Tampa, FL\nFocus: Node.js (70%) and React.js (30%)\nTechnology environment: MongoDB, PostgreSQL, Druid, and Cassandra\nAbout The Company\nHAN Staffing connects professionals with technology opportunities across a range of industries. For this position, the company is seeking a developer with experience building server-side applications and RESTful APIs using Node.js, together with the ability to contribute to React.js development. The role offers an opportunity to work with a varied data platform that includes both relational and NoSQL technologies. The job information lists Iselin, New Jersey, as the location and also identifies Irving, Texas, or Tampa, Florida, as potential role locations. Candidates should confirm the applicable work location and arrangement during the hiring process.\nAbout The Role\nHAN Staffing is seeking a Node.js Developer to contribute to the design, development, and support of scalable API services and web applications. The position is primarily focused on Node.js, which represents approximately 70% of the work, with React.js accounting for approximately 30%. You will collaborate with other technical team members to implement application features, connect services to databases, and deliver reliable solutions aligned with project needs. This opportunity is suited to a developer with one to two or more years of total professional experience and at least one year of relevant Node.js API experience. The successful candidate will bring a practical understanding of JavaScript and an interest in building maintainable software.\nQualifications\nOne to two or more years of total professional software development experience.\nAt least one year of relevant experience developing APIs with Node.js.\nWorking knowledge of JavaScript and server-side development concepts.\nExperience implementing RESTful APIs and understanding of API design principles, including clear resource structures, appropriate HTTP methods, and reliable error handling.\nExposure to React.js and the ability to contribute to frontend development as required.\nFamiliarity with one or more of the following data technologies: MongoDB, PostgreSQL, Druid, or Cassandra.\nUnderstanding of how applications interact with databases and external services.\nAbility to communicate effectively, work collaboratively, and contribute to shared development goals.\nCareful approach to code quality, troubleshooting, and documenting technical work.\nResponsibilities\nDevelop, enhance, and maintain Node.js services and RESTful APIs designed for scalability, reliability, and ease of maintenance.\nContribute to application development across a workload that is approximately 70% Node.js and 30% React.js.\nBuild and update server-side features, API endpoints, and supporting application components based on project requirements.\nIntegrate services with data stores such as MongoDB, PostgreSQL, Druid, and Cassandra, as applicable to the project.\nWork with team members to clarify technical requirements and deliver functional, well-tested solutions.\nIdentify and troubleshoot defects, performance issues, and integration challenges across application services.\nFollow established development practices and contribute to readable, maintainable code.\nParticipate in code reviews, testing, and technical discussions to support consistent implementation and product quality.\nCommunicate progress, raise risks, and document relevant implementation details for the team.\nBenefits\nSpecific compensation, benefits, and employment arrangements were not provided in the available job details. HAN Staffing can share applicable information about pay, benefits eligibility, work schedule, and employment terms during the recruitment process. Candidates are also encouraged to confirm whether the position is based in Iselin, Irving, or Tampa and whether any onsite, hybrid, or remote arrangements are available.\nEqual Opportunity\nHAN Staffing is committed to fair and inclusive hiring practices. Applicants will be considered based on their qualifications, experience, and ability to meet the requirements of the role, without discrimination on any basis protected by applicable law. Candidates who need an accommodation during the application or interview process are encouraged to contact the recruiting representative.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4490083055": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Jamf, we believe in an open, flexible culture based on respect and trust. Our track record and thriving work environment all stem from the freedom we grant ourselves to get the job done right. We take pride in helping tens of thousands of customers around the globe succeed with Apple.\nThe secret to our success lies in our connectivity, while operating with a high degree of flexibility. Work-life balance remains our priority while feeling connected is important to maintain our strong culture, achieve our goals, and thrive as #OneJamf.\nWhat you'll do at Jamf:\nThe Associate Software Engineer is responsible for building the tools required to help organizations succeed with Apple.\nCollaborate with experienced Engineers, Product Management and leadership to understand priorities and how those solve problems. Subject matter expert in various Jamf components and product offerings.\nYou may be required to work periodically at a Jamf office or collaborative work location with other Jamf employees in your area for certain events or moments that matter.\nWhat you can expect to do in this role :\nCollaborate with more experienced engineers when needed\nEfficiently use available tools with guidance\nLearn and follow engineering best practices and processes while being able to explain deviation\nPartner with senior engineers to understand technical concepts\nMaintain a positive attitude while working through challenges\nWhat we are looking for:\nMinimum of 1 year of experience developing enterprise grade software with understanding of testing and quality assurance processes. (Preferred)\nExperience in current programming language and tools based on position (Preferred)\nExperience with TypeScript, including building or maintaining production code (Preferred)\nHands-on experience with AWS Lambda and other AWS services (Preferred)\nWorking knowledge of Agile development practices, such as sprints, backlog grooming, and standups (Preferred)\nHands-on experience with AI-driven coding assistants like GitHub Copilot, Cursor, others to enhance development productivity.\nExperience developing with AI tools, such as building AI-enabled features or applications, not just using coding assistants (Preferred)\nHighschool Diploma / GED (Required)\n4 years / Bachelor's Degree (Preferred)\nA combination of relevant experience and education may be considered\nSecurity And Privacy Requirements\nParticipation in ongoing security training is mandatory\nEstablished security protocols will be adhered to, sensitive data will be handled responsibly, and data protection practices are followed, including understanding relevant privacy regulations and reporting breaches\nAcknowledging the Jamf Code of Conduct, where applicable security and privacy policies can be found, is a requirement of all roles at Jamf\nHow we help you reach your best potential:\nNamed a 2025 Best Companies to Work For by U.S. News\nNamed a 2024 Best Technology Company to Work For by U.S. News\nNamed one of Forbes Most Trusted Companies in 2024\nNamed a 2024 Best Companies to Work For by U.S. News\nOur developers work in agile delivery teams to produce new features, improve software components, and are the subject matter experts for our Jamf product offerings.\nYou will have the opportunity to make a real and meaningful impact for more than 75,000 global customers with the best Apple device management solution in the world.\nWe constantly push the boundaries of technology, our developers support new innovations and OS releases the moment they are made available by Apple.\nSeveral Jamf engineers are named in patents and with team names like CatDog, ThunderSnow and Dalek you can expect to have some fun while building cutting-edge software.\nYou will have the opportunity to work with a small and empowered team where the culture is based on trust, ownership, and respect.\nWe offer a clear career path that enables you to grow under supportive leadership and management\nVisit our Jamf Engineering blog to learn more about the innovative projects our team is working on and what we learn from each challenge we solve. A blog written by engineers, for engineers at medium.com/jamf-engineering\n22 of 25 world’s most valuable brands rely on Jamf to do their best work (as ranked by Forbes).\nOver 100,000 Jamf Nation users, the largest online IT community in the world.\nPay Transparency\nAt Jamf, base pay is one part of our total compensation package and is set within a defined range. These ranges can vary based on hiring location. Where an individual's pay falls within that range depends on several factors, including role scope, location, budget, skills, experience, and qualifications. This approach helps ensure fair, competitive pay and provides room to grow as you develop in your role.\nThe national pay transparency range below represents all U.S. locations and accounts for geographic differences in pay, resulting in a broader range.\nNational Pay Transparency Range\n$64,800—$117,480 USD\nWhat it means to be a Jamf?\nWe are a team of free-thinkers, can-doers, and problem-crushers. We value humility and the relentless pursuit of knowledge. Our culture flows from a spirit of selflessness and relentless self-improvement - driving both personal growth and collective progress throughout our company. We unite around common goals while respecting personal approaches, believing that fulfilled individuals create a thriving, vibrant workplace.\nOur aim is simple: hire exceptionally good people who are incredibly good at what they do and let them do it. We provide the support and resources to let everyone be their authentic, best selves at work, at rest, and at play. We are committed to supporting the continual improvement of Apple in the workplace, the organizations that rely on them and the people who keep it all running smoothly.\nAbove it all, waves our banner of #OneJamf – and the knowledge that when we stand together, we accomplish so much more than we could alone. We seek individuals who share this unwavering journey toward growth to join us in our quest for constant improvement.\nWhat does Jamf do?\nJamf extends the legendary Apple experience people enjoy in their personal lives to the workplace. We believe the experience of using a device at work or school should feel the same, and be as secure as, using a personal device. With Jamf, customers are able to confidently automate Mac, iPad, iPhone and Apple TV deployment, management, and security – anytime, anywhere – to protect the data and applications used by employees in the workplace, students learning in the classroom, and streamline communications in healthcare between patients and providers. More than 2,500 Jamf strong worldwide, we are free-thinkers, can-doers, and problems crushers who are encouraged to bring their whole selves to work each and every day.\nGet social with us and follow the conversation at #OneJamf\nJamf is committed to creating an inclusive & supportive work environment for all candidates and employees. Candidates with disabilities or religious beliefs are encouraged to reach out if they need additional support or alternative options to our recruiting processes to accommodate their disability or religious belief. If you need an accommodation, please contact your Recruiter or Recruiting Coordinator directly. Requests for accommodation will be handled confidentially by Recruiting and will not be shared with the hiring manager. Jamf is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against individuals who request reasonable accommodation for disability or religious beliefs. To request accommodations please email us at recruiting@jamf.com",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4490083612": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "What We Need\nCORPAY is looking to hire a Junior Full Stack Software Developer. In this role, you will help develop and maintain software that supports our foreign exchange and e-commerce platforms. You will work alongside experienced Developers, Product Owners, QA, and Scrum Masters to turn business needs into reliable technology solutions. This is a great opportunity for someone early in their development career who is eager to build hands-on experience in full-stack development within the financial technology industry.\nHow We Work\nTo set you up for success, we provide:\nAssigned workspace for your home-office setup\nCompany-issued equipment and remote access\nFormal, hands-on training and support from experienced team members\nRole Responsibilities\nAssisting with developing and maintaining front-end and back-end application features.\nWriting clean, maintainable, and well-tested code with guidance from senior developers.\nParticipating in Agile ceremonies, including stand-ups, sprint planning, and retrospectives.\nCollaborating with Product Owners, Developers, QA, and Scrum Masters to understand requirements and complete assigned work.\nSupporting troubleshooting, debugging, and resolving technical issues.\nBuilding and consuming HTTP-based APIs and integrations.\nParticipating in code reviews and applying feedback to improve development skills and code quality.\nFollowing established development practices, including unit testing, clean code, version control, and continuous integration.\nLearning new technologies and contributing ideas to improve applications and team processes.\nQualifications & Skills\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field; equivalent practical experience will also be considered.\n1–3 years of professional software development experience, internships, co-ops, or relevant project experience.\nFoundational experience with .NET and C# development.\nFamiliarity with JavaScript and/or TypeScript.\nBasic understanding of SQL Server, relational databases, and database design.\nExperience or familiarity with web applications and HTTP-based APIs.\nUnderstanding of software-development fundamentals, including testing, debugging, source control, and Agile ways of working.\nStrong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\nComfortable working both independently and collaboratively within a close-knit development team.\nCurious, motivated, and eager to learn new technologies and apply them appropriately.\nExperience in payments, foreign exchange, e-commerce, or financial technology is a plus but not required.\nAbout Corpay\nCorpay is a global technology organization that is leading the future of commercial payments with a culture of innovation that drives us to constantly create new and better ways to pay. Our specialized payment solutions help businesses control, simplify, and secure payment for fuel, general payables, toll and lodging expenses. Millions of people in over 80 countries around the world use our solutions for their payments.\nAt Corpay, we are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful workplace where employees are valued for their diverse perspectives, experiences, and contributions. We believe that diversity, equity, and inclusion strengthen our teams, drive innovation, and support our continued success globally.\nAs part of our hiring process, offers of employment may be subject to the successful completion of pre-employment screening conducted by an authorized third-party provider, in accordance with applicable laws and Corpay policies. Screening requirements may include employment references, identity verification, criminal record checks, financial or sanctions screening, and other background checks relevant to the role and permitted by local law.\nNotice to Recruitment Agencies and Search Firms: Corpay does not accept unsolicited resumes from agencies or search firms without a valid written agreement in place. Any unsolicited candidate submissions will become the property of Corpay, and no fees will be paid related to such submissions.\nLearn more about Corpay: https://www.corpay.com\nTransparency & Compliance\nEqual Opportunity Employer\nCorpay is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, age, disability, marital status, genetic information, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Corpay is committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where individuals are respected and valued for their diverse perspectives, experiences, and contributions. If you require reasonable accommodation during any part of the application or interview process, please notify a representative of the Human Resources Department.\nUse of Artificial Intelligence in Hiring\nCorpay may use artificial intelligence (AI) and other technology-enabled tools to support certain aspects of the recruitment process, such as application screening, candidate assessment, or interview scheduling. These tools are designed to enhance efficiency, consistency, and fairness throughout the hiring process. AI tools do not make final hiring decisions. All employment decisions involve human review. Corpay is committed to the responsible use of AI, including appropriate oversight and safeguards designed to support fair and unbiased outcomes.\nCandidate Privacy Notice\nFor information about how Corpay processes personal information during the recruitment process, please review our Candidate Privacy Notice: https://www.corpay.com/privacy-policy.\nPay Philosophy\nCorpay is committed to fair, equitable, and transparent compensation practices. Compensation decisions are based on objective, job-related factors including skills, experience, qualifications, and market benchmarks. Where required by applicable law, salary or compensation ranges will be included in the job posting or provided prior to the interview process, where required by applicable law. Additional compensation elements such as bonuses, incentives, benefits, or variable pay may apply where applicable.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4455407005": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Company\nCareem is building the Everything App for the greater Middle East — making it easy to move around, order food and groceries, manage payments, and more. Our purpose is simple: to simplify and improve people’s lives and build an awesome organisation that inspires.\nSince 2012, Careem has enabled earnings for over 2.5 million Captains, simplified the lives of more than 70 million customers, and built a platform where the region’s best talent and entrepreneurs thrive. We operate in 70+ cities across 10 countries, from Morocco to Pakistan.\nWe’re now entering our next chapter — one powered by AI. We’re looking for AI talent: curious problem-solvers who know how to apply AI to build tools, automate workflows, and create real impact. Whether it’s streamlining operations, enhancing customer experience, or reimagining internal systems — we want people who can make Careem work smarter and move faster.\nAbout the team\nAt Careem, the mission for the NextGen program is to help grow our new joint Engineering by learning how to write Clean Code, use SOLID principle techniques, and design reliable systems. The ultimate goal is to train the new Engineers to build Engineering excellence foundations with high standards. Our program covers all the areas of Careem tech be it Cyber Security, Data, Infrastructure, and all the Software Engineering tracks like Backend, Frontend as well as Mobile.\nWe are looking for software engineers to join our team of talented engineers that share a common interest in distributed backend systems, their scalability, and continued development. You will work alongside a top talent for an accelerated learning path. You will have access to some of the most exciting projects and advanced tech for accelerated learning and exposure.\nYou will be responsible for maintaining some of our services that power the Careem Engine, scaling highly distributed systems, and continuously documenting and improving our engineering practices. These large-scale, distributed systems handle everything from user requests to payment processing.\nWhat you'll do:\nResponsibilities\nOur tech stack is Java 8 and Spring Boot, Micro-Service Architecture, SQL and no-SQL DBs, and AWS infrastructure. Key responsibilities include:\nDevelopment of our distributed backend system to meet the challenging functional, scalability, and reliability requirements for our fast-growing business.\nMaintain features and systems, with an emphasis on code quality, maintainability, readability, and testing.\nFacilitate collaboration with other engineers, product owners, and designers to solve interesting and challenging problems across our platform.\nBe a valued member of an autonomous, cross-functional agile team.\nYou care about quality and you know what it means to ship high-quality code.\nWhat you'll need:\nFresh graduates are encouraged to apply!\nThe ideal candidate will have a passionate commitment to improving the lives of people, an insane focus on excellence and customer service, and a strong alignment with our core values: being bold, focused, agile and collaborative.\nMust have:\nBachelor's Degree in Computer Science or other related technical fields.\nUnderstanding of Object-oriented design, data structures, and algorithms.\nAbility to solve complex problems.\nMust be able to write clean and maintainable code (must love coding!).\nAbility to effectively articulate technical challenges and solutions; deal with loosely defined problems and fast-changing requirements & think abstractly.\nPassionate about learning new technologies and working on a product of massive scale and impact.\nAble to communicate effectively.\nAttention to detail.\nNice to have:\nKnowledge of AWS\nKnowledge of clean code principles\nDeep understanding of design patterns\nDemonstrated ability of test-driven development",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4472229647": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "[ Quora is a privately held, \"remote-first\" company . This position can be performed remotely from anywhere in Canada or the United States. Please visit careers.quora.com/eligible-countries for details regarding employment eligibility by country.]\nAbout Quora\nQuora’s mission is to grow the world's collective intelligence. To do so, we have two platforms:\nQuora: a global knowledge sharing platform with millions of monthly unique visitors, bringing people together to share insights on various topics and providing a unique platform to learn and connect with others.\nPoe: a cloud workspace where millions of users run multiple AI agents on shared context and tools. One subscription, every frontier model, and the collaboration layer that makes them work together.\nBehind these products are passionate, collaborative, and high-performing global teams. We have a culture rooted in transparency, idea-sharing, and experimentation that allows us to celebrate success and grow together through meaningful work. Join us on this journey to create a positive impact and make a significant change in the world.\nThis role will be working on our Quora product.\nAbout The Team And Role\nMachine Learning is central to Quora's mission of growing the world's collective intelligence. We have 100+ Machine Learning models in production powering various product features. We use a variety of algorithms — everything from linear models to decision trees and deep neural networks. Our production models operate at a huge scale, serving hundreds of millions of people using Quora every month.\nOur team owns Quora's ML platform and ranking infrastructure across four areas: serving reliability, ML engineer enablement and developer velocity, business impact, and cost efficiency . We want to empower all ML engineers at Quora to be as impactful as they can be in solving different ML problems at scale.\nAs a Software Engineer (New Grad) on this team, you'll work at the intersection of machine learning, distributed systems, and GPU serving performance — and your work will have an enormous impact on Quora's long-term success.\nNo previous ML infrastructure experience is required for this role. You'll be joining a team of senior and staff engineers, learning this stack from the people who built it, with a dedicated mentor and strong technical guidance — and you'll be shipping to production in your first few weeks.\nStack: Python, Go, C++, PyTorch, Kubernetes/EKS, NVIDIA Triton, Ray, AWS\n🚀 Excited to see our MLP team's amazing work in action? Check out some of the incredible projects they've completed below! 👇✨\nhttps://quoraengineering.quora.com/Migrating-from-x86-to-AWS-Graviton-A-Journey-in-Cost-Optimization-and-Performance\nhttps://aws.amazon.com/blogs/containers/quora-3x-faster-machine-learning-25-lower-costs-with-nvidia-triton-on-amazon-eks/\nhttps://quoraengineering.quora.com/Building-a-Service-Mesh-in-a-Hybrid-Environment\nhttps://quoraengineering.quora.com/Building-Embedding-Search-at-Quora\nhttps://quoraengineering.quora.com/Feature-Engineering-at-Quora-with-Alchemy\nResponsibilities\nHelp build and maintain the core infrastructure that powers Quora's ML platform, ensuring high availability, scalability, and performance\nBuild and improve the distributed systems that serve our ML models in production, from Large Recommendation Models (LRMs) to Large Language Models (LLMs)\nWork on GPU model serving, optimizing latency, throughput, and cost to support larger and more capable models\nContribute to platform initiatives such as PyTorch-first standardization and ML ecosystem modernization\nImprove ML developer velocity by building tooling that helps ML engineers develop, test, and deploy models more efficiently\nModernize our feature store so ML engineers can get new features into production faster\nParticipate in the team's on-call rotation, helping resolve production issues as you grow your knowledge and ownership of the platform\nMinimum Requirements\nAvailability for meetings and impromptu communication during Quora's \"coordination hours\" (Mon-Fri: 9am-3pm Pacific Time)\nA 2025 or 2026 graduate with or pursuing a B.S., M.S., or Ph.D. in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field\nGenuine interest in large-scale distributed systems, infrastructure, and machine learning\nKnowledge of Python, Go, or C++, or the ability to learn them quickly\nA passion for learning and always improving yourself and the team around you\nPreferred Requirements\nPrevious software engineering experience via an internship, work experience, open-source contribution, or coding competition\nCoursework or hands-on experience with ML frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow\nExposure to Kubernetes, Docker, or cloud technologies like AWS\nExperience with low-level performance work of any kind: profiling, benchmarking, optimization\nPassion for Quora's mission and goals\nAt Quora, we value diversity and inclusivity and welcome individuals from all backgrounds, including marginalized or underrepresented groups in tech, to apply for our job openings. We encourage all candidates who share a passion for growing the world’s knowledge, even those who may not strictly meet all the preferred requirements, to apply, as we know that a diverse range of perspectives can have a significant impact on our products and our culture.\nAdditional Information\nWe are accepting applications on an ongoing basis. This role is a backfill for an existing vacancy.\nQuora offers a wide range of benefits including medical/dental/vision coverage, equity refreshers, remote work reimbursement, paid time off, employee assistance programs, and more. Benefits are country-specific and may vary.\nThere are many factors that will determine the starting compensation, including but not limited to experience, location, education, and business needs.\nUS candidates only: For US based applicants, the salary range is $97,600 - $139,000 USD + equity + benefits.\nCanada candidates only: For Toronto and Vancouver based applicants, the salary range is $125,320 - $142,783 CAD + equity + benefits. For all other locations in Canada, the salary range is $116,965 - $133,264 CAD + equity + benefits.\nIn equity-eligible countries, we currently also offer a flexible equity program where a portion of equity compensation may be taken as cash.\nWe are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.\nAI technology may assist in sorting applications and recording interview notes, but all decisions are made by a member of our team.\nTo ensure a secure hiring process, all final candidates will undergo identity verification and a comprehensive background check prior to onboarding.\nJob Applicant Privacy Notice: https://careers.quora.com/quora-global-job-applicant-privacy-notice",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4475045317": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Opportunity\nJoin our talent network and connect with U.S. clients for flexible, project-based development work as an Agentic Software Engineer (Google Antigravity).\nYou will integrate directly into our client's team and work alongside their existing designers and engineers on a daily basis.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with a deep understanding of full-stack architectures (e.g., Java, Python, C#, React, Node, etc.).\n1-3 years of professional experience using Google Antigravity as a primary development environment to coordinate AI-driven implementation across large, multi-file systems while maintaining architectural oversight.\nExperience delivering production software where AI systems generate the majority of implementation code.\nStrong context engineering skills, including structuring codebases, specifications, and documentation to produce reliable, context-efficient AI output.\nAbility to translate complex product requirements into machine-executable, AI-friendly specifications.\nExperience designing AI-first development workflows from specification through deployment.\nAbility to systematically improve AI-generated output through structured iteration and feedback loops.\nComfort working across multiple stacks, using AI to deliver high-quality, production-ready systems.\nExperience operating across frontend, backend, and infrastructure in AI-accelerated environments.\nDisciplined human-in-the-loop review practices, with risk-adjusted validation for high-impact or safety-critical flows.\nStrong curiosity and initiative in evaluating and adopting emerging AI-native engineering practices.\nAdvanced understanding of Agile methodologies and Lean principles and participation in team ceremonies as well as asynchronous work.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients and dedicate yourself to delivering on commitments.\nAbility to consistently work 40 hours per week.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the country of this job posting on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive pay.\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nOpportunity to grow and expand your career.\nOur talent network is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive, and accessible environment where IT professionals can find opportunities that match their skills. We welcome individuals of all races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, national origins, abilities, and experiences. Our focus is on connecting talent with projects based on qualifications, ensuring a fair and transparent process that values diverse perspectives and global collaboration.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482124719": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Position\nForward Deployed Engineers sit inside the client’s problem, not next to it. You embed with an enterprise team, find the work that actually warrants AI, architect the system, build it, and stay long enough to make it survive contact with production.\nThis is a three-way role: consultant, operator, engineer. You should be as comfortable pressure-testing a business case with a COO or VP of Engineering as you are diagnosing why retrieval quality collapsed after a data refresh. The people who succeed here can hold a discovery conversation on Monday and ship what they scoped on Thursday.\nOn this track, your edge is data, retrieval, and model behavior: you make agents trustworthy by getting the data, context, and evaluation right.\nWe work with regulated industries and Fortune 500 clients who have AI mandates, real constraints, and low tolerance for demos that don’t hold up.\nHow We Approach The Work\nFDEs are trusted to shape the solution, not only deliver it. Every engagement calls for architect-level judgment:\nReframes the request. Treats “we need an agent for X” as a hypothesis, not a spec.\nDecomposes the problem. Outcome → process → decisions → data → systems → actors → constraints — before choosing technology.\nChooses the intervention. Remove, simplify, traditional software, automation, LLM, RAG, agent, or multi-agent — and defends why.\nOwns the architecture decision. Documents trade-offs (ADRs), sets success metrics, pushes back on scope that won’t deliver value.\nConsultative Discovery\nClients rarely arrive with a fully formed problem, and the FDE’s first contribution is helping them see it clearly. You lead discovery with genuine curiosity, moving the conversation from stated requirements to underlying needs, and you build credibility through the depth of your understanding rather than the breadth of your pitch.\nUncovers business drivers. What outcome matters, what it’s worth, why now, and what happens if nothing changes.\nUncovers personal drivers. What each stakeholder is measured on, what they’re worried about, and what a win looks like for them individually.\nSurfaces constraints early. Security, compliance, data access, budget, skills, politics, timelines — the things that kill projects in month two.\nAligns stakeholders. Spots conflicting goals between business, engineering, and risk, and brings them to a shared definition of success.\nAsks strategic questions. Follows the answer with “why,” “how do you know,” and “what happens today when…” — without interrogating. Clients leave the conversation understanding their own problem better.\nEarns authority through depth. Credibility comes from the quality of the questions and the insight in the playback, not from pitching technology.\nWhat You'll Do\nDiscover. Run workshops and process discovery with business, data, and engineering stakeholders. Assess data readiness honestly. Separate genuine AI problems from workflow problems wearing an AI costume.\nStructure the process and the spec. For any business process being automated, map the current state, decision points, data inputs, and exceptions, then turn it into specifications that both people and AI systems can execute against reliably.\nArchitect & design. Design agentic systems end to end with emphasis on context and retrieval architecture — data sourcing, chunking, embeddings, hybrid search, reranking, permissions-aware retrieval, knowledge graphs where warranted — plus orchestration, MCP/tool integration, guardrails, and human-in-the-loop checkpoints.\nBuild. Ship working systems — agents, retrieval services, evaluation tooling, and the data flows that feed them. Prototypes that prove value in weeks, not slideware.\nEngineer the delivery system. Own CI/CD for what you build, extended to AI: prompt and context versioning, eval suites that run in the pipeline and gate releases.\nOperate (Day 2). Own what happens after launch — eval harnesses, groundedness and retrieval metrics, observability and tracing, cost and latency management, drift, and the handoff that lets the client’s team run it without you.\nConsult. Present to and defend decisions in front of CTOs, VPs of Engineering, CDOs, and business leadership. Quantify impact in their terms. Support pre-sales scoping and proposal work when the deal calls for it.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with core proficiency in Python (or TypeScript/Node.js).\nHas shipped at least one agentic AI solution, LLM workflow, or RAG architecture to a production environment.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nDemonstrated hands-on experience using AI developer tools (such as Cursor, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, or OpenAI Codex) in daily workflows.\nTrack record of leading client-facing discovery calls to translate unstructured business requirements into technical architectures.\nHands-on experience designing and integrating RESTful APIs, microservices, or event-driven architectures.\nExperience building agentic systems using orchestration frameworks or APIs such as LangGraph, LangChain, n8n, Model Context Protocol (MCP), or direct LLM APIs.\nProven experience taking full end-to-end technical ownership of features from discovery to deployment.\nAbility to work through new and difficult issues and contribute to libraries as needed.\nAbility to create and maintain continuous integration and delivery of applications.\nForensic attention to detail.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nExperience working on Agile / Scrum teams.\nMeaningful experience working on large, complex systems.\nAbility to take extreme ownership over your work. Every day is a challenge to ensure you are performing to the expectations you and your team have agreed upon.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients, and dedicate yourself to delivering on the commitments you and your team make to them.\nStrong Plus\nProduction AI operations (Day 2): eval harnesses, observability and tracing, cost and token economics, drift, debugging non-deterministic systems.\nPrompt- and eval-level regression testing running in CI and gating releases.\nDelivery in regulated environments (financial services, healthcare, insurance, manufacturing).\nPre-sales support: discovery calls, SOW and estimate shaping, technical proposal defense.\nProcess mining, operations analysis, or transformation consulting background.\nClient enablement and training — building the client team’s capability, not just the system.\nPrior consulting or agency environment; comfort with ambiguity and multiple accounts.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the country of this job posting on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive pay.\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nOpportunity to grow and expand your career.\nOur talent network is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive, and accessible environment where IT professionals can find opportunities that match their skills. We welcome individuals of all races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, national origins, abilities, and experiences. Our focus is on connecting talent with projects based on qualifications, ensuring a fair and transparent process that values diverse perspectives and global collaboration.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482178713": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About FullStack\nFullStack is your AI-native engineering partner, built to turn AI capability into certainty. Most companies can demo AI; few can get it to production and prove what it produced. We close that gap with three capabilities, AI built into your products from the start, elite vetted talent who apply it, and transparent execution that shows value every step of the way. With now over 600 customers in North America, FullStack is one integrated partner for all your AI engineering needs. With FullStack, you move forward with confidence.\nWe’re Most Proud Of\nOffering life-changing career opportunities to talented software professionals across the Americas.\nBuilding highly-skilled software development teams for hundreds of the world’s greatest companies.\nHaving delivered hundreds of successful custom software solutions, which have positively impacted the lives and careers of millions of users.\nOur 4.1-star rating on GlassDoor.\nOur client Net Promoter Score of 68, twice the industry average.\nThe Position\nForward Deployed Engineers sit inside the client’s problem, not next to it. You embed with an enterprise team, find the work that actually warrants AI, architect the system, build it, and make it hold up in the real environment.\nThis is a three-way role: consultant, operator, engineer . You should be as comfortable pressure-testing a business case with a COO or VP of Engineering as you are debugging why an agent’s tool-calling loop degraded after a context change. The people who succeed here can hold a discovery conversation on Monday and ship what they scoped on Thursday.\nOn this track, your edge is application engineering: you make agents real inside the client’s actual systems, workflows, and delivery pipelines.\nWe work with regulated industries and Fortune 500 clients who have AI mandates, real constraints, and low tolerance for demos that don’t hold up.\nHow We Approach The Work\nFDEs are trusted to shape the solution, not only deliver it. Every engagement calls for architect-level judgment:\nReframes the request. Treats “we need an agent for X” as a hypothesis, not a spec.\nDecomposes the problem. Outcome → process → decisions → data → systems → actors → constraints — before choosing technology.\nChooses the intervention. Remove, simplify, traditional software, automation, LLM, RAG, agent, or multi-agent — and defends why.\nOwns the architecture decision. Documents trade-offs (ADRs), sets success metrics, pushes back on scope that won’t deliver value.\nConsultative Discovery\nClients rarely arrive with a fully formed problem, and the FDE’s first contribution is helping them see it clearly. You lead discovery with genuine curiosity, moving the conversation from stated requirements to underlying needs, and you build credibility through the depth of your understanding rather than the breadth of your pitch.\nUncovers business drivers. What outcome matters, what it’s worth, why now, and what happens if nothing changes.\nUncovers personal drivers. What each stakeholder is measured on, what they’re worried about, and what a win looks like for them individually.\nSurfaces constraints early. Security, compliance, data access, budget, skills, politics, timelines — the things that kill projects in month two.\nAligns stakeholders. Spots conflicting goals between business, engineering, and risk, and brings them to a shared definition of success.\nAsks strategic questions. Follows the answer with “why,” “how do you know,” and “what happens today when…” — without interrogating. Clients leave the conversation understanding their own problem better.\nEarns authority through depth. Credibility comes from the quality of the questions and the insight in the playback, not from pitching technology.\nWhat You'll Do\nDiscover. Run workshops and process discovery with business and engineering stakeholders. Separate genuine AI problems from workflow problems wearing an AI costume. Come back with a scoped, defensible point of view.\nStructure the process and the spec. For any business or engineering process being automated, map the current state, decision points, and exceptions, then turn it into specifications that both people and AI systems can execute against reliably.\nArchitect & design. Design agentic systems end to end — orchestration, context and retrieval architecture, tool and MCP integration, guardrails, human-in-the-loop checkpoints, and the boundaries between deterministic and non-deterministic components.\nBuild. Ship working systems — agents, multi-step automations, internal tooling, integration layers. You are hands-on. Prototypes that prove value in weeks, not slideware.\nEngineer the delivery system. Own CI/CD for what you build: build, test, release, environments.\nConsult. Present to and defend decisions in front of CTOs, VPs of Engineering, and business leadership. Quantify impact in their terms. Support pre-sales scoping and proposal work when the deal calls for it.\nWhat We're Looking For\n5+ years of professional software development experience with at least one mainstream production stack (TypeScript/Node.js, Python, Java, C#/.NET, or Go).\n1 - 4 years of professional experience building and shipping LLM-powered and agentic AI systems beyond prototypes or demos.\nAdvanced English is required.\nSuccessful completion of a four-year college degree is required.\nHands-on experience with frontier AI developer tools including Cursor, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, or OpenAI Codex.\nProven experience evaluating current-state environments and defining technical roadmaps.\nDemonstrated experience with APIs, service design, event-driven and distributed systems, and data modeling.\nExperience designing and owning CI/CD pipelines, including build, test, release, environments, and deployment processes.\nStrong understanding of context and specification engineering to produce reliable AI output.\nSolid understanding of enterprise integration patterns, including APIs, webhooks, event streams, iPaaS platforms such as n8n or MuleSoft, and MCP.\nTrack record of leading client-facing discovery calls, asking \"why\" before \"how\" to decompose unstructured business problems.\nSkilled at exercising end-to-end delivery ownership and managing project scope without requiring product manager supervision.\nAbility to work through new and difficult issues and contribute to libraries as needed.\nAbility to create and maintain continuous integration and delivery of applications.\nForensic attention to detail.\nA positive mindset and a can-do attitude.\nExperience working on Agile / Scrum teams.\nMeaningful experience working on large, complex systems.\nAbility to take extreme ownership over your work. Every day is a challenge to ensure you are performing to the expectations you and your team have agreed upon.\nAbility to identify with the goals of FullStack's clients, and dedicate yourself to delivering on the commitments you and your team make to them.\nStrong Plus\nProduction AI operations (Day 2): eval harnesses, observability and tracing, cost and token economics, drift, debugging non-deterministic systems.\nPrompt- and eval-level regression testing running in CI and gating releases.\nDelivery in regulated environments (financial services, healthcare, insurance, manufacturing).\nPre-sales support: discovery calls, SOW and estimate shaping, technical proposal defense.\nProcess mining, operations analysis, or transformation consulting background.\nClient enablement and training — building the client team’s capability, not just the system.\nPrior consulting or agency environment; comfort with ambiguity and multiple accounts.\nWork Authorization Requirements\nApplicants must be currently authorized to work in the country of this job posting on a full-time basis.\nFullStack will not sponsor applicants for work visas now or in the future.\nWhat We Offer\nCompetitive pay.\n100% remote work.\nThe ability to work with leading startups and Fortune 500 companies.\nContinuing education opportunities.\nOpportunity to grow and expand your career.\nOur talent network is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive, and accessible environment where IT professionals can find opportunities that match their skills. We welcome individuals of all races, religions, genders, sexual orientations, national origins, abilities, and experiences. Our focus is on connecting talent with projects based on qualifications, ensuring a fair and transparent process that values diverse perspectives and global collaboration.\nLearn more about our Applicants Privacy Notice.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486161894": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Zyte, we don't just collect web data—we solve complex web data challenges at scale. We are a globally distributed team that is bold, curious, and dedicated to building innovative ways to deliver clean, reliable web data from across the internet.\nData is our passion: We unlock access to open web data, empowering organizations—from startups to global enterprises—to power competitive intelligence, analytics, and AI pipelines\nRemote-first culture: Work from anywhere in the world. With over 260 Zytans across 33 countries, our strength comes from diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and skills\nEngineering excellence: We love diving deep into complex code bases, evaluating emerging technologies, and pushing technical boundaries. If you thrive on creative problem-solving and reliably delivering production-grade solutions, you will fit right in\nEstablished system design framework: We systematically analyze functional and product requirements alongside architectural trade-offs to make informed, sustainable design decisions\nReal-world distributed systems challenges: Tackle rare engineering problems in custom networking, high-throughput streaming, and large-scale orchestration under real-world operational constraints\nStrong product ownership: Work on a profitable, market-leading platform with dedicated time and resources allocated for architectural research and strategic feature engineering\nWhy This Role?\nZyte API fetches the web through a ladder of routes: plain HTTP, headless browsers, and, for the hardest targets, Edge—our own residential network of real devices. Edge is the tier that must succeed when everything else has failed. Today, a Rust peer on residential Windows PCs long-polls a single command-and-control service (CNC) over mTLS gRPC; CNC schedules fetches onto peers, runs a CONNECT proxy gateway, owns geo-routing, per-site cooldowns, and bandwidth quotas. It must grow from thousands of nodes to tens of millions of requests a day with rock-solid reliability.\nThe Edge Platform squad owns the control plane and data plane of this residential stack across Windows, Android, and Linux. The next step is building a proper Fleet Manager: a control plane with provider adapters (volunteer PCs, mobile-IP device farms, self-hosted nodes), a reconciler, rollout control, and metrics export sitting beside CNC as the data plane. You will design and operate that system—handling the scheduling, networking, proxying, and reliability work that turns residential devices into infrastructure other squads depend on. You will work directly with the Team Lead, a Principal Engineer, and partner engineering squads across Zyte.\nWhat You'll Do\nScale the data plane. Evolve CNC from a single-replica service into a horizontally scalable fetch scheduler: node selection that respects geo, site cooldowns, jail and per-peer quotas while avoiding detectable patterns, at 50-100M requests per day\nBuild the Fleet Manager control plane. Design and ship the inventory, health, configuration and software-rollout plane for the fleet: provider adapters, a reconciler, a rollout controller and an exporter to BigQuery, so a second device provider can be onboarded without bespoke scripts\nOwn the proxy path. Operate and improve the CONNECT proxy gateway and session handling on the edge, and work with the API squad on IP reputation, proxy leases and request scheduling so Edge slots cleanly into the platform's proxy plane\nEngineer the networking. mTLS gRPC between control plane and peers, long-poll and streaming semantics over unreliable residential links, NAT and carrier-grade NAT behaviour, and bandwidth accounting that is correct under contention\nMake it reliable. Define SLOs for availability, success and latency of the Edge route; build the metrics on peer count, drop-off and bandwidth that hold us and our supply partners accountable; run blue/green rollouts of CNC and peers safely\nShare production ownership. Take part in the squad's on-call rotation, lead incident post-mortems and turn operational lessons into platform improvements\nRaise the bar. Write RFDs for scheduling, fleet management and failover; review designs across the squad; and bring distributed-systems rigour (consistency, backpressure, idempotency, blast radius) to a young codebase\nRequirements\nWho You Are\n5+ years of production Rust experience, shipping and operating services you own end to end\nDistributed systems: you have designed and run schedulers, control planes or stateful services at scale, and can reason about consistency, partitions, backpressure and idempotency without a whiteboard\nDeep networking: TCP, TLS and HTTP at the handshake and packet level, gRPC and long-lived connections across NAT and lossy links, and what a client looks like on the wire\nProxy expertise: you have built or operated forward proxies, proxy gateways or residential/ISP proxy infrastructure, and understand IP reputation, session stickiness and pool health\nOps and reliability experience: SLOs and error budgets, observability you built yourself, production incidents you led, and comfort with being on call\nCross-platform awareness: comfortable with Rust running on Windows, Linux and Android targets, and with FFI boundaries when the data plane needs them\nAsync communication: strong written communication for a globally distributed, remote-first environment\nCurious problem solver: you like finding out why a system behaves the way it does under load, and fixing the cause rather than the symptom\nOur Tech Stack\nLanguages: Rust (tokio, tonic), C++ (Cronet) at the peer boundary; Python and Java in the services we integrate with\nProtocols: gRPC and protobuf over mTLS, HTTP CONNECT proxying, the Chromium network stack and our own browserless HTTP client\nInfrastructure: GCP and Kubernetes for the control plane, Terraform, blue/green deployments; multi-cloud (OCI, GCP) and data centres (Hetzner, Servers.com) across the wider platform\nData & Messaging: Valkey, BigQuery, Confluent Kafka\nMonitoring & Observability: Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, OpenTelemetry\nBonus Points\nMobile or desktop Rust: experience shipping Rust on Android, Windows or macOS, or binding Rust to C/C++ via FFI\nFleet or device management: reconcilers, rollout controllers, IoT or volunteer-computing fleets\nAnti-bot and fingerprinting: understanding of how TLS, HTTP and IP signals are used to classify traffic\nWeb scraping & crawling experience: familiarity with the technical challenges of large-scale web data extraction\nOpen source contributions: history of contributing to Rust, networking or distributed-systems open-source projects\nWhy Join Us?\nImpact at scale: Build the residential network tier behind web-scale data pipelines for top-tier global enterprises\nAutonomy and flexibility: Enjoy a genuine remote-first culture with flexible working hours and high organizational trust\nContinuous innovation: Solve emerging, complex technical challenges as AI and web data extraction rapidly evolve\nGlobal community: Collaborate with a passionate, diverse team of distributed systems engineers and data specialists across the world\nIf you are a Rust engineer who wants to turn tens of thousands of residential devices into dependable infrastructure, we would love to hear from you. Join us in building the fleet behind web data extraction at Zyte.\nBenefits\nBy joining the Zyte team, you will:\nBecome part of a self-motivated, progressive, multi-cultural team\nHave the freedom and flexibility to work from where you do your best work\nAttend conferences and meet with team members from across the globe\nWork with cutting-edge open source technologies and tools",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487447757": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Purpose\n- Key Result Areas\n- Uses his/her technical expertise and experience to contribute to all sprint events (planning, refinements, retrospectives, demos)\n- Consults with the team about what is needed to fulfil the functional and non-functional requirements of the IT product to be developed\n- Develops the IT product, performs the unit test in line with the customer’s wishes and IT area’s internal ambitions and reviews colleagues’ IT products.\n- Designs, builds and tests IT products (functional, performance, resilience and security tests) and automates them.\n- Performs Life Cycle Management (including decommissioning) for IT products under management\n- Improves the Continuous Delivery process\n- Resolves incidents and problems relating to IT products under management (including stack)\n- Sets up the IT environment, deploys the IT product on the IT infrastructure and implements the required changes\n- Sets up monitoring of IT product usage by the customer\nOperating Environment, Framework and Boundaries, Working Relationships- The Front End developer is responsible for transforming the design and the product vision into working products and will directly influence how users will interact with the system. The Front End developer works hard to stay on top of fast changing technology and invests a lot of energy in learning new tricks. They are not only caught up on industry trends in client development frameworks but also know what the near future will bring. A love for clean interfaces and a passion for great user experiences goes without saying\n- Works within a multidisciplinary team or in an environment in which multidisciplinary teamwork is carried out.\n- Is primarily responsible for the production (or technical\nconfiguration) of software applications.\n- The range of tasks includes the following:\n- the analysis and design of the application(or the technical configuration);\n- coding applications and/or package integration in one programming languages, scripting languages and frameworks:\n- HTML, CSS/LESS/SCSS/etc., JavaScript, and responsive design\n- Mobile development experience with either native or web-to-native tooling and frameworks\n- JavaScript frameworks and libraries specifically React\n- Understanding of RESTful APIs and how use them in practice\n- Knowledge of Object-Oriented programing\n- Continuous Delivery (Compile, Build, Package, Deploy);\n- Test-Driven Development (TDD) and test automation (e.g. regression, functional and integration tests); debugging and profiling;\n- software configuration management and version control.\n- Be an active participant in grooming and planning, to ensure that acceptance criteria are clear\n- Sit together with designers, SMEs and Product Owner while user stories are developed, bringing input\n- Work in an agile/scrum environment, meeting sprint commitments and contributing to the agile process\n- Maintain traceability of testing activities\nProblem Solving\n- Ability to handle challenges and multi-task, in a high pressure & demanding environment\nDecision Making Authority & Responsibility\n- Take ownership of key decisions, ensuring alignment with organizational goals and stakeholder expectations\nKnowledge, Skills and Experience\n- Past experience as a frontend developer building modern JavaScript-based web applications\n- Expert experience with HTML, CSS/LESS/SCSS/etc., JavaScript, and responsive design\n- Mobile development experience with either native or web-to-native tooling and frameworks\n- Experience using JavaScript frameworks and libraries specifically React\n- Understanding of RESTful APIs and how use them in practice\n- Knowledge of Object-Oriented programing\n- Ability to write effective unit, integration, and end-user automation tests\n- Strong understanding of Agile methodologies\n- Experience as a Developer on a cross-functional agile team preferred\n- Strong communication skills with ability to communicate complex technical concepts and align organization on decisions\n- Sound problem-solving skills with the ability to quickly process complex information and present it clearly and simply\n- Utilizes team collaboration to create innovative solutions efficiently\n- Passionate about technology and excited about the impact of emerging /\ndisruptive technologies\n- Wants to unleash inner self-starter and work in an environment that fosters\nentrepreneurial minds\n- Believes in culture of transparency and trust\n- Open to learning new ideas outside scope or knowledge skillset\n- Problem Analysis\n- Professional expertise/market focus",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487470092": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "We are looking for a Front-End Engineer who is motivated to combine the art of design with the art of programming. Responsibilities will include translation of the UI/UX design wireframes to actual code that will produce visual elements of the application. You will work with the UI/UX designer and bridge the gap between graphical design and technical implementation, taking an active role on both sides and defining how the application looks as well as how it works. Job Responsibilities\nDevelop new user-facing features.\nEnsure the technical feasibility of UI/UX designs.\nOptimize application for maximum speed and scalability.\nWork in multidisciplinary team with other professionals such as back-end developers.\nBuild high-quality mockups and design different prototypes.\nProvide high-quality graphics and visual elements.\nMaintain and improve Solutioninn website.\nSkills Required\nProficient understanding of web markup, including HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap.\nBasic understanding of server-side CSS pre-processing platforms, such as LESS and SASS.\nProficient understanding of client-side scripting and JavaScript frameworks, including jQuery.\nEnable to design responsive and pixel perfect web pages.\nA quick learner who wants to surround himself with a team.\nAn ability to perform well in a fast-paced environment.\nExcellent analytical, multitasking, time-management, interpersonal and communication skills\nGood understanding of advanced JavaScript libraries and frameworks, such as ReactJS, AngularJS is a plus\nBasic knowledge of image authoring tools, to be able to crop, resize, or perform small adjustments on an image. Familiarity with tools such as Photoshop is a plus.\nProficient understanding of cross-browser compatibility issues and ways to work around them.\nProficient understanding of code versioning tools, such as Git.\nGood understanding of SEO principles and ensuring that application will adhere to them.\nRequired Qualifications\nBachelor’s Degree in Computer Science or Software engineering with good CGPA.\nJob Experience\n2 years\nOther Benefits\nBonuses\nCompany Profit Sharing\nFlexible Work Environment\nMedical Coverage\nPetrol Allowance\nLunch Facility\nJob Working Hours 10AM to 7PM Equal Employment Opportunities We provide Equal Employment Opportunities (EEO) to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, national origin, age, disability or genetics. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including recruiting, hiring, placement, promotion, termination, compensation, and training.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487862669": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Canonical is a leading provider of open source software and operating systems to the global enterprise and technology markets. Our platform, Ubuntu, is very widely used in breakthrough enterprise initiatives such as public cloud, data science, AI, engineering innovation and IoT. Our customers include the world's leading public cloud and silicon providers, and industry leaders in many sectors. The company is a pioneer of global distributed collaboration, with 1200+ colleagues in 75+ countries and very few office-based roles. Teams meet two to four times yearly in person, in interesting locations around the world, to align on strategy and execution.\nThe company is founder-led, profitable, and growing.\nCanonical’s Partner Engineering Team is looking for open-source enthusiasts to work across the full Linux stack to ensure new silicon technologies, such as new hardware accelerators, AI stacks, confidential computing, networking, virtualization, and containerization stacks, are optimized for new silicons.\nPartner Engineering works closely with worldwide silicon companies to optimize Ubuntu for their new silicon, from x86, ARM, RISC-V, PowerPC and s390x architectures.\nLocation: This is a Globally remote role\nThe role entails\nCollaborating proactively within a distributed team\nFostering a software ecosystem with seamless user experience for all Ubuntu users\nEvaluating contributions of other engineers to maintain high-quality software standards.\nPlaying a role in shaping the future of Ubuntu via both - new ideas in your areas of interest and advising on work being done elsewhere\nCollaborating with other teams in the Ubuntu and Debian communities, with upstream projects, and commercially supported customers\nDebugging issues on open source code and team maintained code.\nHelping our our customers to integrate their apps, SDKs, build OS images, optimize applications with Ubuntu Core, Desktop and Server\nWorking with a team to maintain Ubuntu, silicon features, and silicon-optimized packages across platforms and technologies such as:\nServers, HPC and AI systems, IoT devices, PCs, SmartNICs and automotive systems\nAI stacks\nGraphics, audio and multimedia stacks\nVirtualisation and Containers\nHardware enablement stacks\nNew architectures, architecture variants and optimized toolchains\nPackage management and dependencies\nPlatform security (secure boot, FDE, Ubuntu Core, Confidential Computing)\nWork from home with global travel 2 to 4 weeks for internal events\nWhat we are looking for in you\nExceptional academic track record from both high school and university\nUndergraduate degree in a technical subject or a compelling narrative about your alternative chosen path\nYou love technology and working with brilliant people\nYou are curious, flexible, articulate, and accountable\nYou value soft skills and are passionate, enterprising, thoughtful, and self-motivated\nYou value building partnerships with a diverse set of internal and external groups\nStrong fundamentals in C, C++ and Python\nExperience or interest in learning Linux distribution packaging\nExperience or Interest in open source maintenance or contribution and licenses\nFundamental understanding of package management and dependency resolution\nAdditional Skills That You Might Also Bring\nExperience with one or more of the following:\nGraphics, audio, or multimedia stacks\nVirtualization and containers (Docker, OCI, Kubernetes)\nHardware enablement for platforms and devices, including SmartNICs, NVMe storage, GPUs, audio components, and sensors\nPerformance optimization\nToolchain development and maintenance\nNetworking protocols and technologies (TCP/IP, DHCP, HTTP/REST)\nSecurity best practices\nIoT and embedded systems, including board-level hardware, SoCs, BMCs, bootloaders, firmware, operating systems, applications, and services\nWhat we offer colleagues\nWe consider geographical location, experience, and performance in shaping compensation worldwide. We revisit compensation annually (and more often for graduates and associates) to ensure we recognize outstanding performance. In addition to base pay, we offer a performance-driven annual bonus or commission. We provide all team members with additional benefits which reflect our values and ideals. We balance our programs to meet local needs and ensure fairness globally.\nDistributed work environment with twice-yearly team sprints in person\nPersonal learning and development budget of USD 2,000 per year\nAnnual compensation review\nRecognition rewards\nAnnual holiday leave\nMaternity and paternity leave\nTeam Member Assistance Program & Wellness Platform\nOpportunity to travel to new locations to meet colleagues\nPriority Pass and travel upgrades for long-haul company events\nAbout Canonical\nCanonical is a pioneering tech firm that is at the forefront of the global move to open source. As the company that publishes Ubuntu, one of the most important open source projects and the platform for AI, IoT and the cloud, we are changing the world on a daily basis. We recruit on a global basis and set a very high standard for people joining the company. We expect excellence - in order to succeed, we need to be the best at what we do. Canonical has been a remote-first company since its inception in 2004. Working here is a step into the future, and will challenge you to think differently, work smarter, learn new skills, and raise your game.\nCanonical is an equal opportunity employer\nWe are proud to foster a workplace free from discrimination. Diversity of experience, perspectives, and background create a better work environment and better products. Whatever your identity, we will give your application fair consideration.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488242914": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThe organization operates within the healthcare sector, addressing the challenges of improving patient care and healthcare delivery through a collaborative and integrated team approach. With a presence across 900 practices nationwide serving over 14.5 million patients annually, the organization focuses on transforming healthcare from within by fostering a culture centered on collective achievements and community impact.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER I role involves full lifecycle software application development to support the organization's healthcare initiatives. This position contributes by developing, testing, and deploying software solutions, participating in Agile processes, and supporting production environments. The role also engages in research and development activities related to generative AI, enhancing the organization's technological capabilities and operational efficiency.\nResponsibilities:\nParticipate in software application and business logic development.\nEngage in Agile/Scrum sessions and project planning.\nConduct code reviews, write code and tests.\nContribute to generative AI research and development.\nAssist with deployment, testing, and validation on QA environments.\nSupport production deployment, validation, troubleshooting, and support.\nMonitor applications and automate processes.\nRequirements:\nBachelor’s degree in information technology or related field.\nPreferably one year of software development experience.\nFamiliarity with generative AI technology preferred.\nExperience with Microsoft Azure platform tools preferred.\nKnowledge of programming languages such as C#, Java, or Python.\nUnderstanding of databases, operating systems, and MS SQL.\nExperience with RESTful APIs, database programming, and UI programming.\nAbility to write maintainable code in C# and SQL.\nWillingness to learn new technologies quickly.\nExposure to CSS, Powershell, JavaScript.\nBasic knowledge of machine learning and generative AI concepts.\nExperience with version control systems like GitHub and familiarity with CI/CD.\nUnderstanding of Agile methodologies is a plus.\nAbility to work collaboratively and communicate effectively in English.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nBase salary range is $69,520 to $86,900, excluding fringe benefits and potential bonuses.\nEligibility to participate in an annual corporate success sharing bonus based on organizational performance.\nFinal compensation depends on skills, education, and experience.\nBenefits & Perks:\nSuperior health plan options\nDental and vision insurance\nHealth savings and flexible spending accounts\nLife and accidental death and dismemberment coverage\n401(k) retirement savings plan with matching and profit-sharing contributions\nGenerous paid time off starting at 3 to 4 weeks annually\nStudent loan refinancing discounts\nProfessional and career development programs\nEmployee assistance program and travel assistance\nWellness programs\nFlexible work hours\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488260076": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThe organization operates in the financial technology sector, focusing on accounts payable automation. It addresses challenges related to reducing costs, preventing overpayments, detecting fraud, and ensuring policy compliance throughout the invoice-to-payment process. By leveraging AI technology, the company supports finance teams in managing these complex workflows effectively.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER role is designed for an early-to-mid-career professional seeking significant ownership and growth within a small engineering team. This position involves developing and maintaining backend features, addressing production issues, and enhancing system reliability for a mature financial platform. The engineer will play a key role in delivering secure, accurate, and efficient solutions that directly impact customer experience and operational integrity.\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop, test, and maintain backend product features primarily using Python, Django, and relational databases.\nUtilize AI-assisted coding tools for problem investigation, implementation, testing, and documentation improvement.\nCritically evaluate AI-generated code for correctness, security, and performance.\nTranslate customer feedback into actionable technical problems and solutions.\nManage tasks from investigation through deployment and follow-up.\nBuild and maintain APIs, asynchronous jobs, integrations, internal tools, and data workflows.\nWrite clear, maintainable code with automated test coverage.\nParticipate in code reviews and technical discussions.\nEnhance system reliability, observability, documentation, and development processes.\nEnsure financial correctness, data integrity, and customer privacy.\nTake increasing ownership of features and technical decisions.\nRequirements:\nEarly-to-mid-career professional software engineering experience.\nStrong Python programming skills.\nExperience with relational databases including design, querying, and debugging.\nFamiliarity with APIs, automated testing, Git, and collaborative development.\nExperience using AI-assisted coding tools responsibly.\nStrong debugging skills and attention to data impact.\nUnderstanding of application concerns like authorization, concurrency, retries, and failure handling.\nClear written and verbal communication.\nCareful approach to handling sensitive financial data.\nComfortable with broad ownership in a small team environment.\nCuriosity, humility, and willingness to learn.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nSalary Range: USD 130,000 to 155,000 per year plus annual bonus.\nBenefits & Perks:\nMedical, Dental, and Vision insurance for employees and their families.\nEmployer-sponsored 401(k) plan with company match.\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488261051": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "We're hiring 10 Full-Stack Engineers at CCRIPT.\nLocation: On-site, Islamabad or Lahore\nHours: New York hours, full-time. That's 6 PM – 3 AM in Pakistan.\nPay: Salary on the 1st. Your share of client revenue on the 15th. That's Commissions.\nLevel: Mid to senior\nWe don't want people who only build to a ticket. We want engineers who can take a product from an idea to something real users depend on, and own all of it: the interface, the API, the database and the deploy.\nIf you've only ever worked on one side of the stack, this isn't for you. If you've shipped full products that people use every day, keep reading.\nWhat you'll do\n• Build and ship web products with TypeScript, React and Next.js on the front and Node.js on the back\n• Design data models and APIs, and work with Postgres\n• Build fast, clean, accessible interfaces that work on any screen\n• Integrate LLM APIs and AI features into real products\n• Deploy and run what you build with Docker, CI/CD and the cloud\n• Use AI tools (Claude, Cursor, Copilot, agents) every day to ship faster and better. We pay for them.\n• Own your features after launch: monitor them, fix what breaks and keep improving them\nWhat we're looking for\n• Mid to senior experience as a full-stack engineer, with products running in production\n• Strong TypeScript, React and Next.js, and Node.js on the server\n• Solid with SQL databases, ideally Postgres, and with designing APIs\n• You care about the details users notice: speed, polish and things that just work\n• Experience with Docker, CI/CD and a cloud like AWS\n• Experience building with LLM APIs is a big plus\n• You pick up new frameworks and tools fast\n• AI tools are already part of how you work\n• High ownership. You finish what you start and fix what's broken.\nThe basics\n• A 20% raise every year\n• A new MacBook\n• Your AI tools, on us\n• Health insurance\n• All-day food, on the company\n• Luxury gym membership\n• 24 paid days off\n• Travel and rental allowance\n• Retirement benefit (EOBI)\nHow to apply\nApplying takes 2–5 minutes: a short, casual video on why you fit.\nApply here: https://careers.ccript.com/careers/ae391a4c-3747-4f0f-9ee4-681b2c843333",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488838083": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Description\nYuzee connects people with education, careers and employment opportunities. Our platform brings together course discovery, job search, institutions, employers and AI-assisted guidance across web and mobile.\nWe’re looking for a senior, hands-on Angular developer who can take ownership of frontend delivery and help guide our technical direction. You should be comfortable understanding an existing product, identifying what needs improvement and delivering practical, reliable solutions.\nAre you a talented and experienced Angular Developer looking to be part of a dynamic and innovative team? Join us at Yuzee and contribute to the creation of cutting-edge web application that redefine user experiences.\nJob Description\nWhat you’ll do\nDevelop and improve our Angular web applications and contribute to our Ionic/Capacitor mobile app.\nOwn features from understanding requirements through implementation, testing and release verification.\nImprove important user journeys, including search, navigation, conversations, forms and account management.\nDiagnose problems across the interface, application state, APIs and data, and resolve their underlying causes.\nWork closely with backend developers to build clear API contracts, dependable integrations and useful error handling.\nHelp establish consistent architecture, reusable components, coding standards and appropriate automated tests.\nReview code, document important decisions and support other developers.\nRecommend improvements that balance product needs, maintainability, performance and delivery time.\nWhat We’re Looking For\nStrong experience delivering production applications with Angular, TypeScript, RxJS, HTML and CSS.\nA sound understanding of component design, routing, forms, state management and asynchronous behaviour.\nExperience maintaining and improving an established codebase.\nStrong skills in REST API integration, authentication, session handling and debugging.\nExperience with Git, pull requests, code reviews and automated testing.\nAttention to responsive design, accessibility and consistent behaviour across browsers and devices.\nClear communication and the ability to explain technical decisions and trade-offs.\nEvidence of taking responsibility for working software, including investigating issues after release.\nWhat Success Looks Like\nYou understand how the existing platform fits together, help the team agree on sensible priorities and deliver improvements users can depend on. Your changes preserve working journeys, reduce recurring problems and make future development easier.\nQualifications\nGood spoken and written English proficiency\nBachelor’s Degree in Computer Science or Computer Engineering\n4 years experience with front-end development\nAt least 4 years of proven experience with Angular 7 or 8\nProven work experience investigating issues faced by users, identify the root causes and fixing them\n4 years of experience in using Agile work methodologies\nProficient in CSS, HTML, and writing cross-browser compatible codes\n4 years of extensive programming experience in HTML5, CSS3, SASS and Bootstrap\n4 years of experience with REST APIs\nKnowledge of JavaScript MV-VM/MVC frameworks including Angluar JS\nExtensive experience with Node JS and Express JS is a bonus\nGreat project management skills is a bonus\nAbility to work with a multicultural team\nExcellent communication skills\nCritical thinker and good problem-solver\nAdditional Information\nThis is a full-time remote job (You will work from home)\nChallenging work environment and complex project where you can really grow as a professional\nCompany shares can be offered based on how successful with our products' launch\nPromotions towards better job roles possible after a certain period of time",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488936551": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Overview\nFounded in Dubai in 2016, SQUATWOLF is a gym wear brand made for athletes who push limits, in and out of the gym. What started in the Middle East has grown into a global movement, with customers in 100+ countries. We’re on a mission to elevate the human experience through high-performance gear that drives strength, progress, and purpose.\nYour Role\nWe are looking for a motivated Mobile Application Engineer (React Native) with 1–3 years of experience to join our engineering team. The ideal candidate should have hands-on experience building, maintaining, and improving cross-platform mobile applications for Android and iOS.\nYou will work closely with senior engineers, designers, and backend developers to develop reliable, high-performance mobile applications and deliver an excellent user experience.\nWhat you will do\nDevelop and maintain cross-platform mobile applications using React Native.\nBuild reusable, scalable, and maintainable components using JavaScript or TypeScript.\nIntegrate RESTAPIs and handle asynchronous data, loading states, and error scenarios.\nImplement state management using tools such as Redux Toolkit or React Context.\nCollaborate with UI/UX designers to translate designs into responsive, pixel-perfect interfaces.\nDebug issues, fix bugs, and optimize application performance.\nWork with native Android and iOS configurations when required.\nIntegrate third-party libraries and SDKs, such as Firebase, push notifications, and analytics tools.\nParticipate in code reviews and follow coding standards and best practices.\nAssist with application testing, release builds, and publishing updates to the Google Play Store and Apple App Store.\nWork with Git and participate in Agile development processes.\nWhat we are looking for\n1–3 years of hands-on experience in React Native development.\nGood understanding of JavaScript (ES6+) and TypeScript fundamentals.\nFamiliarity with React concepts, including hooks, functional components, props, and state.\nExperience integrating REST APIs and handling JSON responses.\nUnderstanding of state management solutions such as Redux Toolkit or Context API.\nFamiliarity with navigation libraries, such as React Navigation.\nUnderstanding of mobile application layouts, responsive design, and platform-specific behavior.\nBasic knowledge of Git, debugging, and troubleshooting.\nFamiliarity with Android and iOS development environments.\nGood problem-solving skills and willingness to learn new technologies.\nAbility to work collaboratively in a team environment.\nHands-on experience using AI coding tools such as Cursor and Claude.\nNice to have\nExperience publishing applications to the Google Play Store or Apple App Store.\nFamiliarity withFirebase Analytics, Crashlytics, and push notifications.\nExperience with performance optimisation, caching, and memorymanagement.\nBasic understanding of native Android (Kotlin/Java) or iOS (Swift/Objective-C).\nExperience writing unit tests or component tests.\nWhy SQUATWOLF\nWe reward energy, ownership, and people who take initiative.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488948133": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Overview\nFounded in Dubai in 2016, SQUATWOLF is a gym wear brand made for athletes who push limits, in and out of the gym. What started in the Middle East has grown into a global movement, with customers in 100+ countries. We’re on a mission to elevate the human experience through high-performance gear that drives strength, progress, and purpose.\nYour Role\nWe are looking for a Frontend Engineer (React/ Next.js) with 1–3 years of experience to join our engineering team and help maintain and grow SQUATWOLF’s headless e-commerce store front. You will work closely with a senior engineer, designers, product and backend developers. You will ship UI features, fix bugs, keep the site fast and SEO-friendly, and look after the marketing and analytics integrations the business relies on.\nWhat you will do\nDevelop and maintain a production e-commerce storefront using React and Next.js.\nBuild reusable, maintainable components in TypeScript, styled with Tailwind CSS.\nWork with Server Components, Client Components, layouts, route handlers and Server Actions.\nChoose the right rendering and caching approach (SSR, static, ISR / revalidation, or client-side) foreach page, based on performance and SEO needs.\nIntegrate the Shopify Storefront Graph QL API (products, collections, cart) and our in-house REST API. Handle loading states, caching and errors.\nBuild and maintain a multi-store, multilingual storefront: English and Arabic (RTL), several countries and currencies, and locale-aware routing.\nTurn Figmadesigns into responsive, accessible interfaces that work in both LTR and RTL.\nImprove Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS) through image optimization, code splitting and lazy loading.\nIntegrate and maintain third-party services: tag managers and analytics (GTM, Meta, TikTok, Snapchat, Klaviyo and others), search and recommendations, reviews, loyalty, customer support chat and cross-border commerce.\nDebug issues and ensure the site works across browsers and devices, including the mobile app web view.\nVerify changes for each regional store before release and support QA and product sign-off.\nWhat we are looking for\n1–3 years of hands-on React experience, with practical Next.js experience (App Router preferred).\nGood understanding of JavaScript (ES6+) and TypeScript.\nStrong grasp of React fundamentals: hooks, functional components, props, state and component lifecycle.\nUnderstanding of Next.js routing, data fetching, Server Components vs Client Components, and rendering strategies (SSR, SSG, ISR).\nExperience consuming Graph QL APIs, as well as REST APIs and JSON responses.\nProficiency in HTML5, CSS3and responsive design, with hands-on Tailwind CSS experience.\nExperience with, or a strong interest in, internationalization (i18n), including right-to-left (Arabic) layouts.\nUnderstanding of state management with React Context or similar.\nBasic understanding of web performance and SEO principles.\nComfortable with Git, browser Dev Tools, debugging and troubleshooting.\nCareful, detail-oriented approach to changes on a live, revenue-generating site.\nGood problem-solving skills, willingness to learn, and the ability to work well in a team.\nHands-on experience using AI coding tools such as Cursorand Claude.\nNice to Have\nExperience with the Shopify Storefront API, Shopify customer accounts, or other headless commerce platforms.\nExperience with multi-region or multi-currency e-commerce.\nFamiliarity with analytics and tracking tools (Google Tag Manager, GA4, Meta Pixel / Conversions API, Klaviyo).\nExperience writing unit, component or end-to-end tests (Jest, React Testing Library, Playwright).\nWhy SQUATWOLF\nWe reward energy, ownership, and people who take initiative.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489003621": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company Description\nDarkthorn Labs specializes in designing cutting-edge, efficient software solutions that drive business productivity and enhance customer experiences. We are committed to innovation and quality, helping businesses transform processes and achieve their goals. By leveraging technology, we create tools that have a meaningful impact, empowering organizations to excel in competitive markets.\nRole Description\nThis is a full-time on-site role for a Node.js / React Developer located in Lahore. The role involves designing and developing scalable applications using Node.js and React, building and optimizing both front-end and back-end components, and collaborating with team members to deliver high-quality software solutions. Responsibilities also include maintaining code quality, troubleshooting, and ensuring seamless integration of components.\nQualifications\n- Minimum 3 years of professional experience in either Node.js or React (or both)\n- Proficiency in Front-End Development with React\n- Strong Back-End Web Development skills, particularly in Node.js\n- Expertise in Software Development and JavaScript fundamentals\n- Experience with TypeScript and its practical applications\n- Hands-on experience using AI coding agents such as Claude Code, Cursor, or similar\n- Working knowledge of both SQL and NoSQL databases\n- Experience with Linux systems and AWS (particularly EC2)\n- Ability to write clean, maintainable, and efficient code\n- Strong problem-solving and debugging skills\n- Excellent teamwork and collaboration abilities\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489019857": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Role\nThe role focuses on building the user-facing surface of the product — high-performance web applications in React and TypeScript that serve hundreds of thousands of users daily.\nThe engineer will work closely with designers, backend engineers, and product managers to translate complex requirements into fast, accessible, reliable interfaces, with ownership of component architecture, state management, and rendering performance.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign and build responsive, accessible user interfaces in React, TypeScript, and modern CSS for customer-facing web applications\nArchitect and maintain component libraries and design system integrations, ensuring consistency across product surfaces\nIntegrate with REST and GraphQL APIs, handling caching, optimistic updates, and error/retry strategies in client state management\nDiagnose and resolve performance issues — bundle size, render cost, Core Web Vitals — and establish performance budgets in CI\nWrite comprehensive unit and integration tests using Jest or Vitest and Playwright; maintain CI/CD pipelines for frontend builds and deploys\nConduct code reviews and pair with backend engineers on API contracts, TypeScript types, and data-loading patterns\nCollaborate with designers in Figma to validate implementations and contribute to usability and accessibility improvements (WCAG 2.1 AA)\nWhat We Are Looking For\n3–6 years of professional frontend engineering experience building production web applications at scale\nDeep expertise in React (hooks, suspense, server components) and TypeScript, with strong JavaScript fundamentals\nHands-on experience with state management patterns (Redux Toolkit, Zustand, React Query, or equivalent) and data-fetching libraries\nTrack record of measurable performance work: code splitting, lazy loading, caching strategies, Web Vitals optimization\nComfort with build tooling (Vite or Webpack), package management, and monorepo workflows (Turborepo or Nx)\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience\nBonus: Experience with Next.js, server-side rendering strategies, WebAssembly, or building design systems consumed by multiple teams",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489028393": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Role\nThe role builds the interfaces customers touch every day - complex, data-dense web applications rendered in React and TypeScript, backed by a design system shared across the entire product suite.\nThe engineer will sit at the intersection of design and infrastructure: translating Figma specs into performant, accessible components while collaborating directly with backend engineers on API contracts and GraphQL schemas.\nKey Responsibilities\nBuild and ship production features in React, TypeScript, and Next.js, owning them from design handoff through launch and iteration\nDevelop reusable components for a shared design system used across multiple product surfaces, with strict accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA) and responsive breakpoints\nIntegrate with backend services via REST and GraphQL (Apollo Client), negotiating schemas and driving API contract changes when needed\nOwn frontend performance: bundle analysis, code splitting, lazy loading, Core Web Vitals optimization, and profiling with Lighthouse and React DevTools\nWrite unit and integration tests with Jest, React Testing Library, and Playwright; maintain CI checks that block regressions before merge\nParticipate in code reviews, architecture discussions, and RFC processes that shape frontend standards across the engineering org\nDebug and resolve production issues end-to-end, using Sentry, Datadog RUM, and log analysis to diagnose user-facing failures\nWhat We Are Looking For\n3–6 years of professional frontend engineering experience shipping user-facing products at scale\nDeep proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, React, and modern CSS (Tailwind, CSS-in-JS, or CSS Modules)\nHands-on experience with a modern meta-framework (Next.js, Remix, or equivalent) and client-side state management (Redux, Zustand, or React Query)\nStrong grasp of browser fundamentals: rendering pipelines, caching, async patterns, and the performance implications of each\nTrack record of building accessible interfaces and writing tested, maintainable component code\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience\nBonus: Experience with design systems tooling (Storybook, Figma tokens), WebSockets/realtime UIs, or contributing to open-source frontend libraries",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489042026": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Position: Software Engineer (With SaaS Startup Project Experience)\nExperience: 8–15 years\nEmployment Type: Full-Time\nLocation: Remote\nMANDATORY::\n***Visa: US Citizen & Green Card.\n***EXPERIENCE IN SAAS STARTUP ENVIRONMENT MUST\n***SHOULD HAVE PROPER LINKEDIN WITH GOOD CONNECTIONS\n***MUST HAVE SKILLS: Python, Django, Flask, FastAPI, aiohttp, GraphQL, REST, React, React Native, TypeScript, Redux, Vite, PostgreSQL, Redis, Docker, AWS (ECS, RDS, CloudFront)\nPreferred Technical Skills\nBackend: Python, Django, Flask, FastAPI, aiohttp\nAPI Development: REST, GraphQL\nFrontend: React, React Native, TypeScript, Redux, Vite\nDatabases: PostgreSQL, Redis\nCloud & Infrastructure: AWS ECS, RDS, CloudFront, Docker\nKey Responsibilities\nLead and deliver large-scale backend engineering projects independently, from requirements gathering through deployment.\nDesign and develop scalable, reliable, and high-performance backend systems.\nOwn and improve eligibility processing, identity management, and client configuration systems.\nBuild system architectures that support significant data growth and increasing business demands.\nCollaborate with product managers and internal operations teams to define requirements, business use cases, and edge cases.\nPartner with senior engineering leaders to execute the long-term technical roadmap.\nProvide technical leadership, code reviews, and mentorship to junior engineers.\nIdentify opportunities to improve system performance, reliability, maintainability, and scalability.\nRequired Qualifications\n8–15 years of professional software engineering experience, with strong backend development expertise.\nStaff-level engineering capabilities, including system design, architectural decision-making, and technical leadership.\nStrong hands-on experience with Python and backend frameworks such as Django, Flask, or FastAPI .\nExperience designing and scaling complex backend systems in production environments.\nStrong understanding of REST APIs, GraphQL, databases, and distributed system design.\nExperience with PostgreSQL, Redis, Docker, and AWS cloud services.\nAbility to lead complex projects independently and work effectively with cross-functional teams.\nStrong product mindset with the ability to translate business requirements into technical solutions.\nExperience mentoring engineers and influencing technical decisions across teams.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4490001135": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Position Description & Qualifications\nWe are seeking a Junior Software Engineer to support our Army PPB BOS contract. The candidate will work with the technical lead and development team to maintain and enhance existing Java-based applications in the cloud environment, troubleshoot issues, and support ongoing development and modernization efforts. The position offers opportunities to learn Python, APEX and other application development tools, as well as gain hands-on experience to AI-assisted development practices already being used by the team. Prior experience with AI technologies is not required, we are looking for someone with a solid Java foundation, strong problem-solving skills, and a willingness to learn new technologies. The candidate will be a self-starter, team-player and will be expected to manage and complete their tasks in a fast-paced results driven environment.\nThis position is fully remote, and candidates may be located anywhere within the United States. Candidates must be able to obtain/maintain a Secret security clearance.\nIn This Role, You Will\nContribute to all phases of the development lifecycle.\nWrite well designed, testable, and efficient code.\nCode, design, and implement Java and APEX solutions for the Army.\nConduct software analysis, programming, testing, debugging activities and maintenance.\nDevelop technical designs for application development and recommend changes to improve established application processes.\nTo Be Successful In This Role, You Must Have\nThe ability to obtain/maintain a Secret security clearance.\nU.S. Citizenship.\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science.\n1 year of relevant IT experience.\nExperience with software development lifecycle.\nExperience with Java software design, development, testing, and deployment.\nExperience with web-based applications, client/server applications, or cloud-hosted systems.\nAbility to travel 10%.\nAdditional Desired Qualifications\nExperience with software development concepts and Agile methodologies.\nExperience with common release tracking software (JIRA, Confluence).\nExperience with basic SQL.\nKnowledge of AWS Cloud.\nKnowledge of leveraging AI-assisted development tools, automated code generation, or AI-powered engineering capabilities.\nIf you are interested in working with a dedicated Serco team, then submit your application now for immediate consideration. It only takes a few minutes!\nCompany Overview\nSerco Inc. (Serco) is the Americas division of Serco Group, plc. In North America, Serco’s 9,000+ employees strive to make an impact every day across 100+ sites in the areas of Defense, Citizen Services, and Transportation. We help our clients deliver vital services more efficiently while increasing the satisfaction of their end customers. Serco serves every branch of the U.S. military, numerous U.S. Federal civilian agencies, the Intelligence Community, the Canadian government, state, provincial and local governments, and commercial clients. While your place may look a little different depending on your role, we know you will find yours here. Wherever you work and whatever you do, we invite you to discover your place in our world. Serco is a place you can count on and where you can make an impact because every contribution matters.\nTo review Serco benefits please visit: https://careers.serco-na.com/us/en/what-we-offer. If you require an accommodation with the application process please email: careers@serco-na.com or call the HR Service Desk at 800-628-6458, option 1. Please note, due to EEOC/OFCCP compliance, Serco is unable to accept resumes by email.\nCandidates may be asked to present proof of identity during the selection process. If requested, this will require presentation of a government-issued I.D. (with photo) with name and address that match the information entered on the application. Serco will not take possession of or retain/store the information provided as proof of identity. For more information on how Serco uses your information, please see our Applicant Privacy Policy and Notice.\nSerco does not accept unsolicited resumes through or from search firms or staffing agencies without being a contracted approved vendor. All unsolicited resumes will be considered the property of Serco and will not be obligated to pay a placement or contract fee. If you are interested in becoming an approved vendor at Serco, please email Agencies@serco-na.com.\nSerco is an equal opportunity employer. We evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics.\nPay Transparency\nOur Total Rewards package includes competitive pay, performance-based incentives, and benefits that promote well-being and work-life balance—so you can thrive both professionally and personally. Eligible employees also gain access to a wide range of benefits from comprehensive health coverage and health savings accounts to retirement plans, life and disability insurance, and time-off programs that support work-life balance. Program availability may vary based on factors such as contract type, location, hire date, and applicable collective bargaining agreements.\nSalary range: The range for this position can be found at the top of this posting. This range is provided as a general guideline and represents a good faith estimate across all experience levels. Actual base salary will be determined by a variety of factors, including but not limited to, the scope of the role, relevant experience, job-related knowledge, education and training, key skills, and geographic market considerations. For roles available in multiple states, the range may vary to reflect differences in local labor markets. In addition to base salary, eligible positions may include other forms of compensation such as annual bonuses or long-term incentive opportunities. Benefits – Comprehensible benefits for full-time employees (part-time employees receive a limited package tailored to their role):\nMedical, dental, and vision insurance\nRobust vacation and sick leave benefits, and flexible work arrangements where permitted by role or contract\n401(k) plan that includes employer matching funds\nTuition reimbursement program\nLife insurance and disability coverage\nOptional coverages that can be purchased, including pet insurance, home and auto insurance, additional life and accident insurance, critical illness insurance, group legal, ID theft protection\nBirth, adoption, parental leave benefits\nEmployee Assistance Plan\nTo review all Serco benefits please visit: https://careers.serco-na.com/us/en/about-us.\nSerco complies with all applicable state and local leave laws, including providing time off under the Colorado Healthy Families and Workplaces Act for eligible Colorado residents, in alignment with our policies and benefit plans. The application window for this position is for no more than 60 days. We encourage candidates to apply promptly after the posting date, as the position may close earlier if filled or if the application volume exceeds expectations. Please submit applications exclusively through Serco’s external (or internal) career site. If an applicant has any concerns with job posting compliance, please send an email to: careers@serco-na.com.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4490058567": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:13:29.989030+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Jamf, we believe in an open, flexible culture based on respect and trust. Our track record and thriving work environment all stem from the freedom we grant ourselves to get the job done right. We take pride in helping tens of thousands of customers around the globe succeed with Apple.\nThe secret to our success lies in our connectivity, while operating with a high degree of flexibility. Work-life balance remains our priority while feeling connected is important to maintain our strong culture, achieve our goals, and thrive as #OneJamf.\nWhat you'll do at Jamf:\nThe Associate Software Engineer is responsible for building the tools required to help organizations succeed with Apple.\nCollaborate with experienced Engineers, Product Management and leadership to understand priorities and how those solve problems. Subject matter expert in various Jamf components and product offerings.\nYou may be required to work periodically at a Jamf office or collaborative work location with other Jamf employees in your area for certain events or moments that matter.\nWhat you can expect to do in this role :\nCollaborate with more experienced engineers when needed\nEfficiently use available tools with guidance\nLearn and follow engineering best practices and processes while being able to explain deviation\nPartner with senior engineers to understand technical concepts\nMaintain a positive attitude while working through challenges\nWhat we are looking for:\nMinimum of 1 year of experience developing enterprise grade software with understanding of testing and quality assurance processes. (Preferred)\nExperience with Java, Kotlin, or TypeScript, from coursework, projects, or work experience (Preferred)\nExperience with Angular or another front-end framework (Preferred)\nWorking knowledge of Agile development practices, such as sprints, standups, or ticket-based workflows (Preferred)\nExposure to AWS, including DynamoDB (Preferred)\nFamiliarity with containers, such as Docker, and with GitHub Actions (Preferred)\nHands-on experience with AI-driven coding assistants like GitHub Copilot, Cursor, others to enhance development productivity.\nHighschool Diploma / GED (Required)\n4 years / Bachelor's Degree (Preferred)\nA combination of relevant experience and education may be considered\nSecurity And Privacy Requirements\nParticipation in ongoing security training is mandatory\nEstablished security protocols will be adhered to, sensitive data will be handled responsibly, and data protection practices are followed, including understanding relevant privacy regulations and reporting breaches\nAcknowledging the Jamf Code of Conduct, where applicable security and privacy policies can be found, is a requirement of all roles at Jamf\nHow we help you reach your best potential:\nNamed a 2025 Best Companies to Work For by U.S. News\nNamed a 2024 Best Technology Company to Work For by U.S. News\nNamed one of Forbes Most Trusted Companies in 2024\nNamed a 2024 Best Companies to Work For by U.S. News\nOur developers work in agile delivery teams to produce new features, improve software components, and are the subject matter experts for our Jamf product offerings.\nYou will have the opportunity to make a real and meaningful impact for more than 75,000 global customers with the best Apple device management solution in the world.\nWe constantly push the boundaries of technology, our developers support new innovations and OS releases the moment they are made available by Apple.\nSeveral Jamf engineers are named in patents and with team names like CatDog, ThunderSnow and Dalek you can expect to have some fun while building cutting-edge software.\nYou will have the opportunity to work with a small and empowered team where the culture is based on trust, ownership, and respect.\nWe offer a clear career path that enables you to grow under supportive leadership and management\nVisit our Jamf Engineering blog to learn more about the innovative projects our team is working on and what we learn from each challenge we solve. A blog written by engineers, for engineers at medium.com/jamf-engineering\n22 of 25 world’s most valuable brands rely on Jamf to do their best work (as ranked by Forbes).\nOver 100,000 Jamf Nation users, the largest online IT community in the world.\nPay Transparency\nAt Jamf, base pay is one part of our total compensation package and is set within a defined range. These ranges can vary based on hiring location. Where an individual's pay falls within that range depends on several factors, including role scope, location, budget, skills, experience, and qualifications. This approach helps ensure fair, competitive pay and provides room to grow as you develop in your role.\nThe national pay transparency range below represents all U.S. locations and accounts for geographic differences in pay, resulting in a broader range.\nNational Pay Transparency Range\n$64,800—$117,480 USD\nWhat it means to be a Jamf?\nWe are a team of free-thinkers, can-doers, and problem-crushers. We value humility and the relentless pursuit of knowledge. Our culture flows from a spirit of selflessness and relentless self-improvement - driving both personal growth and collective progress throughout our company. We unite around common goals while respecting personal approaches, believing that fulfilled individuals create a thriving, vibrant workplace.\nOur aim is simple: hire exceptionally good people who are incredibly good at what they do and let them do it. We provide the support and resources to let everyone be their authentic, best selves at work, at rest, and at play. We are committed to supporting the continual improvement of Apple in the workplace, the organizations that rely on them and the people who keep it all running smoothly.\nAbove it all, waves our banner of #OneJamf – and the knowledge that when we stand together, we accomplish so much more than we could alone. We seek individuals who share this unwavering journey toward growth to join us in our quest for constant improvement.\nWhat does Jamf do?\nJamf extends the legendary Apple experience people enjoy in their personal lives to the workplace. We believe the experience of using a device at work or school should feel the same, and be as secure as, using a personal device. With Jamf, customers are able to confidently automate Mac, iPad, iPhone and Apple TV deployment, management, and security – anytime, anywhere – to protect the data and applications used by employees in the workplace, students learning in the classroom, and streamline communications in healthcare between patients and providers. More than 2,500 Jamf strong worldwide, we are free-thinkers, can-doers, and problems crushers who are encouraged to bring their whole selves to work each and every day.\nGet social with us and follow the conversation at #OneJamf\nJamf is committed to creating an inclusive & supportive work environment for all candidates and employees. Candidates with disabilities or religious beliefs are encouraged to reach out if they need additional support or alternative options to our recruiting processes to accommodate their disability or religious belief. If you need an accommodation, please contact your Recruiter or Recruiting Coordinator directly. Requests for accommodation will be handled confidentially by Recruiting and will not be shared with the hiring manager. Jamf is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against individuals who request reasonable accommodation for disability or religious beliefs. To request accommodations please email us at recruiting@jamf.com",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T22:32:02.225929+00:00"
  },
  "cache:posts": {
    "entries": {
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/josephcass_breaking-brookfield-announces-huge-27-billion-share-7523323322541969408-zmpB": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:34:55.386770+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "BREAKING: Brookfield announces HUGE $27 BILLION AI data centre project in the UK! \n\nBrookfield has partnered with British energy company Drax Group and AI business Radiant to develop one of the UK’s largest AI data centres at Drax Power Station in the north of England. \n\nBloomberg reports that the project could attract more than $27 Billion billion in investment, with an initial $3.3 Billion planned for the first phase, backed by Brookfield’s partnership with the Qatar Investment Authority.\n\nThe idea is to build the data centre alongside an existing power station, giving it access to the enormous amounts of electricity needed to run AI technology. Drax CEO Will Gardiner said: “If constructed in full, this project could become one of the largest data centres in the UK.” Brookfield's Connor Teskey recently said of AI infrastructure: \"there is no shortage of capital - and there is no shortage of demand.\"\n\nBig news for European AI infrastructure!\n\nFollow Joseph Cass for finance news and insights.",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-03T10:00:57.048Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/outsideir35_jobsrmine-activity-7525611188022607874-4CSc": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:34:55.386770+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "#hiring Junior Python Developer\n\nApply here: https://lnkd.in/gfTx3__p\n\nJunior Python DeveloperJob Title: Python Engineer Location: UK Based - Fully Remote Salary/Rate: Up to £175 Daily Outside IR35 Start Date: In the next two weeks Job Type: Initial 6 month contactCompany Introduction We have an exciting opportunity now available with one of our sector-leading consultancy clients! They are currently looking for a Python Engineer to join their team for an initial six-month contract.Job Summary:We are seeking a dynamic and passionate Python Developer to join our innovative software development team. In this role, you will be instrumental in designing, developing, and maintaining scalable applications that drive our core business operations. Your expertise will help shape the future of our technology solutions, ensuring high performance, security, and seamless integration with various platforms and services. This position offers an exciting opportunity to work with cutting-edge tools and technologies in a fast-paced environment committed to excellence and continuous improvement.Responsibilities:Develop robust, efficient, and scalable Python-based applications aligned with project requirements and best practices in software development.Collaborate with cross-functional teams to design APIs, web services, and microservices using RESTful principles for seamless data exchange.Integrate Python solutions with cloud platforms such as AWS and Azure to optimize deployment and scalability.Participate in full software development life cycle activities including planning, coding, testing, debugging, and deployment.Write comprehensive unit tests to ensure code quality and maintainability across all projects.Work closely with Front End developers utilizing Angular, React, or Vue.js to create cohesive user experiences using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and TypeScript.Maintain version control using Git or SVN, document code changes thoroughly, and adhere to SDLC",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-09T17:32:06.318Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/trmlabs_at-2005-utc-on-october-29-approximately-activity-7521757016516628480-UBCU": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T22:34:55.386770+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "At 20:05 UTC on October 29, approximately USD 6.36 billion began moving out of Binance wallets across ten blockchains, most of it in about 20 minutes. It is the largest crypto theft on record, roughly four times the Bybit hack of February 2025.\n\nTRM Labs attributes the attack to TraderTraitor, North Korea’s elite state-sponsored hacking unit, based on robust on-chain and off-chain intelligence. The same group was named by the FBI in the Bybit hack, and the staging, the Tornado Cash funding and the pre-signed transactions all match earlier North Korea-linked heists.\n\nThe response has been fast. Tether, Circle, Ripple, World Liberty Financial and Arbitrum’s Security Council have frozen roughly USD 2.7 billion. But the attacker still controls about USD 2.4 billion in assets beyond any issuer’s reach, and is racing to convert and move them.\n\nTRM continues to work with Binance and the Beacon Network to track the funds and alert partners in real time. The story is still developing, and we will share more as the investigation unfolds.\n\nRead our full analysis: https://lnkd.in/e-9KjvPB",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-30T02:17:00.224Z"
        }
      },
      "https://pe.linkedin.com/posts/khursheed-jahan-ara-8baa93110_koderlabs-is-hiring-for-associate-software-activity-7185587254185082880-4FE0": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:16:32.362298+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "KoderLabs is hiring for Associate Software Engineer - Node JS.\n\nLocation: Karachi (Onsite)\nRequirement: Enrolled in final semester of BSCS or Software Engineering. Prior relevant internship experience is a plus.\n\nApply away at jobs@koderlabs.com and mention \"ASE-NodeJS\" in subject line.",
          "posted_at": "2024-04-15T10:38:23.128Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/ahad-khan-hrmanager_were-hiring-nodejs-developer-12-years-activity-7462111595511312384-LkQT": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:16:32.362298+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "🚀 We're Hiring: Node.js Developer (1–2 Years Exp.)\nCompany: Bitrupt\nLocation: Saddar, Karachi (Near Press Club) – On-site\n\nThe Role\nWe aren't looking for a corporate robot. We need a rising backend builder who lives in Node.js, breathes APIs, and is ready to write code that actually impacts real products. If you have 1 to 2 years of solid experience and love solving puzzles behind the screen, let’s talk.\n\nWhat You’ll Bring to the Table\nNode.js Mastery: You know your way around Express.js (or NestJS) and event-driven architecture.\nDatabase Comfort: You can talk to MongoDB or SQL databases without breaking a sweat.\nAPI Crafting: You build clean, secure, and fast RESTful APIs.\nProblem-Solving: You don't just find bugs; you crush them.\n\nWhy Bitrupt?\nWork right in the heart of Karachi (Saddar), easily accessible from anywhere.\nFast-paced environment with zero corporate red tape.\nMassive room for quick professional and financial growth.\n\nDrop Your Specs!\n📧 Email: Send your resume to careers@bitrupt.co\n👉 Use Subject: Node.js Developer - [Your Name]\n📞 WhatsApp / Call: 0303-2518858",
          "posted_at": "2026-05-18T12:07:23.677Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/aimnode-technologies_job-title-backend-developer-location-karachi-activity-7191360107010502656-E1oV": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:16:32.362298+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Job Title: Backend Developer \nLocation: Karachi\nCompany: AimNode Technologies\nJob Type: Full-time\n\nAre you a skilled Backend Developer with expertise in Node.js and/or Laravel? We're looking for someone like you to join our team and contribute to our exciting projects!\n\nResponsibilities:\n- Develop and maintain backend systems using Node.js and/or Laravel frameworks\n- Design and implement RESTful APIs for seamless communication between frontend and backend\n- Collaborate with frontend developers to integrate user-facing elements with server-side logic\n- Optimize performance and scalability of applications to handle high traffic volumes\n- Implement security best practices to safeguard sensitive data and prevent cyber threats\n\nRequirements:\n- Proficiency in Node.js and/or Laravel frameworks with a strong understanding of their core principles\n- Hands-on experience in building and deploying scalable web applications and APIs\n- Familiarity with database systems such as MySQL, MongoDB, or PostgreSQL\n- Solid understanding of frontend technologies like HTML, CSS, and JavaScript\n- Excellent problem-solving skills and ability to troubleshoot complex issues\n\nBenefits:\n- Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package\n- Opportunity for professional growth and career advancement\n- Collaborative and supportive work environment with a focus on innovation\n- Flexible work hours\n\nIf you're passionate about backend development and thrive in a dynamic environment, we want to hear from you! Apply now with your resume and portfolio showcasing your projects and expertise in Node.js and/or Laravel at aimnodetechnologies@gmail.com.\nLet's build something amazing together!",
          "posted_at": "2024-05-01T08:57:38.493Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/aimnode-technologies_job-title-nodejs-developer-location-karachi-activity-7176828931122053120-mDsE": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:16:32.362298+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Job Title: Node.js Developer\nLocation: Karachi\nCompany: AimNode Technologies\nJob Type: Full-time\n\nJob Description:\nWe are seeking a talented Node.js Developer to join our team. As a Node.js Developer, you will be responsible for designing and implementing server-side web application logic, as well as integrating user-facing elements developed by front-end developers. You should have a strong understanding of JavaScript and asynchronous programming. The ideal candidate is passionate about building scalable, high-performance web applications using Node.js and related technologies.\n\nResponsibilities:\n- Develop and maintain server-side logic using Node.js\n- Design and implement RESTful APIs for web services\n- Collaborate with front-end developers to integrate user-facing elements with server-side logic\n- Optimize application performance for maximum speed and scalability\n- Implement security and data protection measures\n- Write clean, maintainable, and testable code\n- Stay up-to-date with emerging technologies and best practices\n\nRequirements:\n- Proven experience as a Node.js Developer or similar role\n- Strong proficiency in JavaScript and asynchronous programming\n- Experience with Node.js frameworks such as Express.js or Koa.js\n- Knowledge of database technologies such as MongoDB, MySQL, or PostgreSQL\n- Familiarity with front-end technologies such as HTML, CSS, and JavaScript\n- Experience with version control systems (e.g., Git)\n- Excellent problem-solving and communication skills\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field (preferred)\n\nHow to Apply:\nInterested candidates should submit their resume, along with a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and why they are a good fit for the position. Please also include links to any relevant portfolios or projects. Applications can be sent to devawaisdeveloper@gmail.com with the subject line \"Node.js Developer.\"",
          "posted_at": "2024-03-22T06:35:56.173Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/haluk-sayar-34635811_cop31-zeroemissionmobility-cop31-share-7524444889644871680-0YvB": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:16:32.362298+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "At COP31, our panel From Climate Targets to Market Deployment: Scaling Zero-Emission Mobility Across Markets will explore how different markets can accelerate the rollout of zero-emission mobility.\n📅 10 November 2026, 13:30–14:15\n📍 Türkiye Pavilion, Room 3, Blue Zone\nAttendance requires COP31 Blue Zone accreditation.\n#COP31 #ZeroEmissionMobility \n \nChris Heron, Ioana Petcu, Feng An, Ph.D., Michiel Langezaal, Kristian Ruby, E-Mobility Europe, Avrasya E-Mobilite Derneği (Eski isim AVERE), Turkish Association for Energy Economics / Enerji Ekonomisi Derneği, International Association for Energy Economics",
          "posted_at": "2026-11-06T12:17:39.424Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/jensen-huang-in-the-matrix-learning-how-ugcPost-7526476851985211392-OLOm": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:16:32.362298+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Jensen Huang in the Matrix, learning how Chinese spies work\n\nWait till the end👀\n\nMade with AI by Arminn_Ai\n▌Editor’s Note —\nMazhar Pasha\n6:08 AM · Nov 12, 2026",
          "posted_at": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/nudrat-imtiaz-63ab5a1b4_karachi-nodejs-onsite-activity-7294672497482866689-fIs3": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:16:32.362298+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "HR Ways - Hiring Tech Talent is hiring Backend (Node.js) Developer in Karachi.\n\nJob Description: \n\nResponsibilities:\n\n- Backend Development: Design, develop, and maintain high-performance backend systems using Rust to build scalable and efficient applications.\n- Blockchain Integration: Work on integrating blockchain protocols and building solutions to enhance decentralized applications (DApps).\n- API Development: Build and maintain RESTful and/or GraphQL APIs to communicate with front-end systems and third-party services.\n- System Architecture: Collaborate with the architecture team to design robust, scalable, and secure backend solutions.\n- Database Management: Optimize and maintain relational and NoSQL databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MongoDB, etc.).\n- Security & Optimization: Ensure code quality, security, and optimize application performance.\n- Collaboration: Work closely with front-end developers, DevOps, and other teams to ensure smooth deployment and integration of features.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Proven experience as a Backend Developer.\n- Experience with Node.js.\n- Strong understanding of blockchain technology, including experience with smart contracts, decentralized systems, and cryptocurrency protocols.\n- Familiarity with Ethereum, Polkadot, Solana, or similar blockchain ecosystems is a plus.\n- Experience with API design and development, both RESTful and GraphQL.\n- Strong knowledge of databases and database optimization techniques.\n- Solid understanding of security best practices in backend and blockchain development.\n- Version control experience (e.g., Git).\n- Familiarity with cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP, Azure) and containerization tools (Docker, Kubernetes) is a plus.\n- Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to work independently as well as part of a team.\n\nBonus Points:\n\n- Experience with smart contract development (Solidity, Rust on Solana, etc.).\n- Knowledge of Web3 and decentralized finance (DeFi) protocols.\n- Contribution to open-source blockchain projects or Rust libraries.\n- Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines and automated testing frameworks.\n\nOther Details:\n\nExperience: 6 months to 1 year\nLocation: Karachi\nWork Mode: Onsite\nWorkdays: Monday - Friday\n\nPlease apply through the below link or you can share your resume at jobs@hrways.co & cc nudrat@hrways.co (not com) with the Subject line ''Backend Developer - Karachi''\n\nLink: https://lnkd.in/dYHmJcrq\n\n#karachi #nodejs #onsite #backend #developer #hrways #hiring #techtalent",
          "posted_at": "2025-02-10T11:04:11.827Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/pakistan-it-jobs_hiring-backend-developer-nodejs-karachi-activity-7389224553194881024-m6qX": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-14T18:16:32.362298+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Hiring: Backend Developer (Node.js) – Karachi, Onsite\nWe’re looking for a passionate Backend Developer with strong expertise in Node.js to join our growing tech team in Karachi.\n\nWhat We’re Looking For:\n2+ years of hands-on experience with Node.js & Express.js\nStrong understanding of APIs, RESTful services & database design (MongoDB/MySQL)\nExperience with version control (Git)\nProblem-solving mindset & teamwork attitude\n\nWhat You’ll Do:\nBuild and maintain scalable backend systems\nCollaborate with frontend and mobile teams\nOptimize APIs for performance and security\n\n📍 Location: Karachi (Onsite)\n 🕒 Job Type: Full-time\nsend your cv at : hr@asoratech.com",
          "posted_at": "2025-10-29T09:00:18.607Z"
        }
      }
    },
